/* Thornwell's new script. Each row owns its opening and all three complete
   reply/answer pairs. The last two rows concern the companion and a later visit.
   No scenery is implied by a speaker's portrait or by an old map placement. */
const THORNWELL_DIALOGUE_CAST = (()=>{
  const cast={};
  const t=(title,first,...replies)=>({title,first,replies});
  const p=(name,role,bio,pre,sight,news,back,bramble,...rows)=>cast[name]={role,bio,pre,sight,news,back,bramble,rows};
  p('Linna','Mill bookkeeper','Linna checks the mill’s accounts and has a dry sense of humour about the work nobody notices until it goes wrong.',
    'Are you looking for someone? I can usually place a name more quickly than a description of their hat.',
    'Oh! I thought someone was bringing a pony through town. That is very definitely a dragon.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then I owe the next person with an unlikely story a more patient hearing.',
    'Corin. How much of your day have you managed to keep for yourself?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. I know his name because Rowan once included dog biscuits in a mill delivery.',
    t('The missing sack','A miller asked me to hide a lost sack in the figures. I told him I could hide a number, but his customer would still be missing flour.',
      ['Did he admit he lost it?','Eventually. The customer accepted a later delivery. We could actually solve the problem once he named it.'],
      ['Was he trying to steal it?','No. He had stacked it on the wrong cart and was embarrassed. Embarrassment can make an ordinary mistake expensive.'],
      ['I would hate telling someone I had lost their food.','So would I. I offered to go with him. He still had to do the talking.']),
    t('Numbers you enjoy','I like adding up a wedding order. For once, a large total means someone expects a happy crowd.',
      ['Do you get invited?','Sometimes. I refuse to calculate the price of the meal while I am eating it.'],
      ['What if they cannot afford enough?','They ask neighbours to bring dishes. Feeding people does not have to be one person’s expense.'],
      ['Nan would want to know who was making the cake.','Then Nan understands the most important figure: how many slices she can reasonably expect.']),
    t('A day without accounts','I tried taking up birdwatching. By the second afternoon I had made a table of sightings. Apparently I bring my work with me.',
      ['That sounds useful for birdwatching.','It is. I was hoping to enjoy something without becoming useful at it.'],
      ['Did you find a favourite bird?','A very untidy rook. It kept spoiling my neat count by arriving after the others.'],
      ['You could leave the paper at home.','I did once. I remembered the birds more clearly than the totals. I may try it again.']),
    t('Another mouth to feed','How are you managing provisions for a dragon? I would rather ask you than turn a guess into town gossip.',
      ['Keeping enough meat takes planning.','Then count meals before the road gets long. A full purse is less useful after the last shop.'],
      ['Sometimes I worry about running short.','That is a sensible worry to act on. Stop among people, check your supplies, and give yourself a margin.'],
      ['I am learning how much he needs.','Keep watching him as well as the supplies. Numbers help, but hunger belongs to a living creature.']),
    t('A return without an errand','You came back to talk. I had started to think every traveller only remembered me when a sum went wrong.',
      ['I wanted to know how you were doing.','Better for being asked. The work is ordinary today, and I am pleased about that.'],
      ['You are allowed to talk about something other than work.','Then I shall complain about my neighbour’s dreadful singing. Affectionately. Mostly.'],
      ['I like having people to come back to.','Then keep making room for visits. A friendship needs more than knowing where someone lives.']));
  p('Garrow','Woodcutter','Garrow is careful about the trees he cuts and more talkative about his mistakes than his successes.',
    'You have the look of someone about to ask a direction. Ask before I send you somewhere you never wanted to go.',
    'Good grief, a dragon. I am going to stand still until I know whether that bothers him.',
    'A dragon has chosen your company? I can understand wanting steady company on a dangerous road.',
    'There you are. I have time for a proper answer if you have a proper question.',
    'That is Rowan’s Bramble. I have had to stop him fetching branches while I was still cutting them.',
    t('Choosing a tree','A straight trunk can hide a rotten centre. I inspect the roots before deciding where a tree will fall.',
      ['Can you always tell?','No. When I am unsure, I leave myself more space and tell everyone else to stand back.'],
      ['Do you ever leave a good tree standing?','Often. A tree shading a spring may be doing a more valuable job than becoming timber.'],
      ['I would be nervous making the first cut.','Good. Keep enough of that feeling to check where your feet are. You do not need to be fearless.']),
    t('The handle I ruined','I once carved an axe handle so carefully that I made it too thin. It broke before I reached the woods.',
      ['At least it broke before you swung it.','Exactly. I was cross at the time. Later I realised how fortunate I had been.'],
      ['Did you make another?','A plainer one. My hands liked it much better than my eyes did.'],
      ['Would you have admitted it to a customer?','I was my own customer. Unfortunately, I complained all evening.']),
    t('A favourite smell','Freshly split wood reminds me of helping my father before I was strong enough to lift much.',
      ['What could you help with?','Stacking kindling. He gave me a real job and checked the stack before he praised it.'],
      ['Did you want to use his axe?','Desperately. He made me wait until I could control it. I appreciate that more now.'],
      ['Do you still think of him while working?','Usually when I catch myself saying something he used to say. It can stop me for a moment.']),
    t('Giving wings room','I keep thinking about how much space your companion needs to spread his wings.',
      ['More than you expect when they are folded.','I will remember that if I meet him on a path. He should not have to squeeze past me.'],
      ['He chooses his way through the trees.','Then I should let him judge the gap. I know timber, not dragon flight.'],
      ['You are more curious than frightened now.','I am both. Getting used to a creature takes more than deciding I ought to be brave.']),
    t('The sound of coming home','I recognise familiar footsteps before I see who is coming. Yours are becoming familiar.',
      ['Is that a good thing?','Yes. Otherwise I would have suddenly remembered urgent work.'],
      ['I never knew my walk had a sound.','Everyone’s does. A dragging heel, a quick turn. You notice when you work with your ears as well as your eyes.'],
      ['I wondered whether you would remember me.','You stopped to listen last time. That is quite enough to remember.']));
  p('Wren','Herbalist and merchant','Wren runs Thornwell’s remedy stall. She is practical about supplies and frank about what she does not know.',
    'Before you buy anything, are you stocking up or trying to solve a particular problem?',
    'A dragon? Oh, let me give him room. Are you both all right, or have you come for supplies?',
    'Thank you for telling me about your companion. I would rather you asked what I know than assumed I could treat a dragon.',
    'Hello again. How has the road been treating you?',
    'That is Bramble. Rowan buys supplies here and usually has to persuade his dog that we are not selling lunch.',
    t('When a remedy fails','People sometimes blame themselves when a remedy does not help. I ask what happened before I suggest buying more.',
      ['What if they used it correctly?','Then repeating the same advice may waste their money. I explain what I do know and where it stops.'],
      ['Do customers dislike hearing that you are unsure?','Some do. I would rather disappoint them with an honest answer than harm them with a confident guess.'],
      ['I am glad I can ask before buying.','Please do. A frightened person should not have to make sense of a shop in a hurry.']),
    t('Your busiest visitor','Berta visits to check my work, then insists she only came because she was passing. She lives close enough for that excuse to be plausible.',
      ['Does the checking annoy you?','Only when she is right before I have had breakfast. I listen anyway.'],
      ['Could you ask her for help directly?','I do. It gives her something definite to do instead of inventing reasons to visit.'],
      ['She must miss working with you.','I think so. I miss having someone to grumble to between customers.']),
    t('Packing for the next town','I prefer travellers to check their Bag while they can still buy supplies. Remembering halfway down the road is less useful.',
      ['What do people forget most?','That supplies get used. Something packed yesterday may not still be there today.'],
      ['I try to save every potion.','Then be careful that saving it does not become a reason to leave yourself badly hurt.'],
      ['I keep enough for the return journey too.','Good. A journey rarely ends at the most distant place you reach.']),
    t('Care for a different creature','I know human remedies. I am not going to pretend that gives me the answer to every problem your dragon might have.',
      ['I can ask him what he needs.','Then start with him. A patient who can explain the problem saves everyone a great deal of guessing.'],
      ['I was hoping you would know everything.','So was I when I first learned this trade. Knowing when to stop guessing was part of learning it.'],
      ['Could I still ask for your advice?','Of course. I can think it through with you without claiming certainty I have not earned.']),
    t('Someone checks on the healer','People ask how my patients are doing. They almost never ask whether I have eaten.',
      ['Have you eaten?','Yes, thank you. You are now ahead of most of my regular customers.'],
      ['Do you forget when you are busy?','Sometimes. Berta is particularly good at detecting when I have skipped lunch.'],
      ['You can remind me, and I can remind you.','Agreed. Neither of us gets to call it fussing when the reminder is deserved.']));
  p('Calder','Fisher and camp keeper','Odo’s grandson Calder keeps a camp on the road between Millwood and Thornwell and helps travellers learn to fish.',
    'Passing through, or taking a breather? Either way, you do not have to keep walking while we talk.',
    'Odo is going to be furious that I met a dragon before he heard about it from me.',
    'A dragon companion! I was going to tell Odo about a large trout. That story may have to wait.',
    'Corin! It is good to see a traveller become a familiar face.',
    'That sounds like Bramble, the hunter Rowan’s dog. Rowan lives in Thornwell.',
    t('Letters to Odo','I leave the frightening parts out of my letters to Odo. Then he visits and asks about exactly those parts.',
      ['How does he know?','Because I suddenly become very detailed about the weather. He has known me too long.'],
      ['Does he worry about you out here?','Yes. He trusts me, but trusting someone does not stop you wanting them safe.'],
      ['You could tell him when the danger has passed.','That would spare me trying to remember which version I sent. You may have a point.']),
    t('A very patient breakfast','I once spent a whole morning fishing before admitting I had forgotten to bait the hook.',
      ['Odo must have enjoyed that story.','He retells it as if he was present. I have stopped correcting the impressive weather he adds.'],
      ['What did you eat instead?','Bread. It was an excellent day to have brought bread.'],
      ['Were you too embarrassed to try again?','For about an hour. Then I was hungry enough to become teachable.']),
    t('Visitors who leave early','Some guests slip away without saying goodbye. I used to wonder if I had done something wrong.',
      ['What changed your mind?','One came back and said he had wanted to let me sleep. I had spent a week being offended by kindness.'],
      ['I sometimes find goodbyes awkward.','A wave is plenty. You do not owe me a speech because I lent you a patch of ground.'],
      ['Do you enjoy meeting so many people?','Yes, though I like the quiet between arrivals too. Both can be true.']),
    t('Fishing with company','Does your companion have the patience to wait while you fish?',
      ['He has his own opinions about waiting.','So does Odo. I appear to collect fishing companions with strong views.'],
      ['I do not always have the patience myself.','Then take breaks. You are allowed to enjoy the water without catching anything.'],
      ['I like having someone beside me.','I understand that. Some of my best afternoons have produced very poor catches.']),
    t('News worth sending home','I ought to write to Odo again. He would like to know you still stop here.',
      ['Tell him I am glad he introduced us.','I will. He will claim arranging it was effortless, which is his usual way of being pleased.'],
      ['Please leave out anything that might worry him.','I will say we had a good talk. That is true, and it belongs in the letter.'],
      ['You should tell him how you are doing too.','Yes. He would notice if I filled an entire letter with somebody else.']));
  p('Merrin','School neighbour','Merrin is an orc who helps people feel at ease around Thornwell’s school and enjoys solving small practical puzzles.',
    'You can ask me a question without apologising first. I promise I have heard stranger ones.',
    'Those are wings. Real wings. Forgive me; I was preparing to say something ordinary.',
    'You are travelling with a dragon? I would have needed a moment even if you had warned me you had surprising news.',
    'Corin, hello. Are you here with a question or an answer today?',
    'Bramble! He belongs to Rowan. The dog has attended more outdoor lessons than some of our students.',
    t('The difficult name','A new pupil asked whether she could call me something easier. I asked whether she wanted me to shorten her name too.',
      ['Did that upset her?','It made her think. Then we practised each other’s names until neither was difficult.'],
      ['Would a nickname have bothered you?','One we both liked would have been fine. Being renamed for someone else’s convenience felt different.'],
      ['I have had people get my name wrong.','Then you know how pleasant it is when someone makes the effort to get it right.']),
    t('A lesson without a winner','I enjoy puzzles people solve together. Some children need practice admitting that another person has a useful idea.',
      ['Do adults need that practice too?','Constantly. Adults are simply better at calling their stubbornness experience.'],
      ['What happens when nobody knows the answer?','We leave it for tomorrow. Confusion is allowed to last longer than a lesson.'],
      ['I like being the one who works it out.','So do I. I try to remember that pleasure when somebody else gets there first.']),
    t('Learning to whistle','I cannot whistle a tune. I can make a noise that causes people to check whether a kettle has boiled.',
      ['Have you asked Linnet to teach you?','I have considered it. I suspect the lesson would test her kindness.'],
      ['Could you sing instead?','Yes, but now I want to whistle. Being bad at something has made me unreasonably determined.'],
      ['I would listen without laughing.','You may laugh if I do. I am learning a tune, not defending my honour.']),
    t('Being stared at','People will stare at your companion. I hope they remember that curiosity is not permission to crowd him.',
      ['I can ask them to step back.','Please do. You do not have to make the request entertaining or apologetic.'],
      ['He is curious about people too.','Then introductions can go both ways. That sounds much more enjoyable for everyone.'],
      ['Did people stare at you here?','Some did when I first arrived. Knowing my name helped them see a neighbour instead of a curiosity.']),
    t('What you bring back','You do not have to return with an extraordinary story every time. An ordinary visit still counts.',
      ['That is a relief.','Good. Tell me about the last meal you enjoyed. We can manage one conversation without a catastrophe.'],
      ['I thought you would want news of the journey.','I do, if you want to tell it. Wanting to hear is different from being owed a report.'],
      ['What would you tell me about your week?','I finally whistled three notes in order. I am trying not to become unbearable about it.']));
  p('Asta','Student of nature','Asta likes testing predictions and is learning to be as interested in a mistake as in a successful experiment.',
    'Could I ask whether it rained on your way here? I am trying to find out how far the last shower travelled.',
    'A dragon! I have so many questions that I cannot choose a sensible first one. Is he comfortable with people coming closer?',
    'A living dragon is your travelling companion? I shall have to practise asking one question at a time.',
    'Hello, Corin. I have discovered another thing I was certain about and wrong about.',
    'I recognise Bramble. Rowan the Hunter is his person; the dog follows him by scent when he remembers to follow anyone at all.',
    t('Predicting rain','I wrote down when I expected rain for a week. My best prediction came from asking someone who had just been outside.',
      ['That sounds like sensible research.','It was useful. It was also a little disappointing after all my careful diagrams.'],
      ['Did the diagrams teach you anything?','Yes: I had been recording clouds without recording which way the wind moved them.'],
      ['What will you try next?','Keeping my observations and my guesses in different columns. I kept forgetting which was which.']),
    t('A question about snails','I wanted to know whether snails found their own way home. They mostly wanted to eat the paper I had numbered.',
      ['Did you find out?','No. I found out that my method needed work and that snails do not respect stationery.'],
      ['Were the snails all right?','Perfectly. I stopped before curiosity became an excuse to keep bothering them.'],
      ['Perhaps ask a question the paper can survive.','That would be an excellent rule for my next experiment.']),
    t('Explaining a mistake','It is surprisingly hard to say “I do not know” after people have called you clever.',
      ['I would rather hear that than a made-up answer.','So would I. I need to give myself the same permission I give other people.'],
      ['Do your teachers mind?','Master Iven asks what I could try next. That makes not knowing feel less final.'],
      ['You still sound clever to me.','Thank you. I am trying to become useful as well as sounding convincing.']),
    t('Questions for a dragon','I want to learn about your companion without making him feel like one of my experiments.',
      ['Then let him decide what he wants to share.','Yes. Curiosity does not make every question welcome.'],
      ['What would you ask first?','Whether he enjoys flying, before I ask how it works. I keep forgetting experience matters too.'],
      ['Some things are private between us.','Understood. You can tell me that without having to explain what those things are.']),
    t('An experiment that worked','I predicted where a puddle would remain longest, and I was right. Nobody else found this thrilling.',
      ['I am listening. What made the difference?','Shade. I had been thinking about depth and ignoring how much sunlight reached the water.'],
      ['Were you pleased?','Ridiculously pleased. I checked three times before allowing myself to celebrate.'],
      ['You can tell me small victories too.','Then you are in danger of receiving very detailed news about puddles.']));
  p('Colm','Local food enthusiast','Colm enjoys cooking for company and has strong, changeable opinions about what makes a satisfying meal.',
    'Have you eaten recently? I ask everyone that, so please do not take it as a comment on your appearance.',
    'Oh. A dragon. I was going to ask whether you were hungry; that question has become more complicated.',
    'You have a dragon to feed as well as yourself? I hope someone remembers to ask whether you have eaten.',
    'Corin! Tell me something pleasant before I invent a reason to complain.',
    'That is Bramble, Rowan’s dog. He remembers everyone who has ever dropped a crumb.',
    t('The dreadful soup','I once tried to rescue a salty soup by adding more of everything else. By supper I could have fed half the town badly.',
      ['Did anyone eat it?','My brother tried. His loyalty survived; his enthusiasm did not.'],
      ['Why not start again?','That would have required admitting defeat before I had used every pot I owned.'],
      ['I have made a mistake worse by trying to hide it.','Then you understand the recipe. The final ingredient is embarrassment.']),
    t('Cooking for strangers','I ask what people dislike before cooking for them. It saves everyone a performance of cheerful suffering.',
      ['What if they say they like everything?','I ask again after mentioning the dish. “Everything” often becomes more specific.'],
      ['I would worry about seeming rude.','A clear answer is kind. I want you to enjoy the meal, not prove you can endure it.'],
      ['What do you refuse to eat?','Anything described as “an interesting mistake” until the cook has swallowed some first.']),
    t('The meal you remember','My favourite meal was bread and onions after helping a neighbour move. I was hungry, tired, and wanted by the people eating with me.',
      ['That sounds better than a royal feast.','It was certainly easier to relax. Nobody cared which hand held the onion.'],
      ['Was the food actually good?','The bread was excellent. I am not giving all the credit to sentiment.'],
      ['I miss eating with Nan.','Tell her that when you see her. People who feed us deserve to know we remember the company too.']),
    t('Dragon table manners','I am curious whether your companion has favourite foods. Everyone talks about what dragons can destroy, and nobody asks what they enjoy.',
      ['He certainly notices a meal.','Then we have a starting point for a friendship, even if we never share a menu.'],
      ['I would rather ask him than guess.','Good. I would be annoyed if someone invented all my preferences from the shape of my teeth.'],
      ['You really can make any subject about food.','I have had years of practice, and now you have supplied a remarkable new subject.']),
    t('A place in the conversation','When you have travelled far, do ordinary conversations start to seem dull?',
      ['They are often exactly what I want.','Then I shall confidently tell you about my ongoing argument with a cabbage recipe.'],
      ['Sometimes I find it hard to settle down.','We can talk slowly. You do not have to arrive in every sense at once.'],
      ['I still want to hear what matters to you.','That is generous. I will try not to mistake it for permission to discuss every meal this week.']));
  p('Rowan the Hunter','Hunter and Bramble’s owner','Rowan shares a home with Ada and hunts with Bramble. Losing track of his dog has made him reconsider how much he takes for granted.',
    'Rowan, at your service. If someone sent you to find the hunter, you have found the right person.',
    'Bramble prepared me for unexpected visitors, but not a dragon. Should I give your companion more room?',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then you know a companion is someone to look after, not something to show off.',
    'Hello, Corin. I am glad you stopped.',
    'Bramble is my dog. If he is following you, thank you for bringing him back.',
    t('When the trail ends','If I lose a trail, I go back to the last mark I trust. Continuing to guess just gives me two problems to untangle.',
      ['Does Bramble understand when you turn back?','He complains with his whole body, then comes along. Usually he finds the scent before I find the mark.'],
      ['How do you decide a mark is real?','Several signs together: disturbed ground, a bent stem, tracks that agree. One broken twig proves very little.'],
      ['I hate feeling as though I have wasted time.','So do I. I have wasted more by refusing to admit I was lost.']),
    t('Ada’s side of the story','Ada says I describe a day in the woods so slowly that she could have walked the route before I finish.',
      ['Is she right?','Absolutely. I include every wrong turn and then explain why it was reasonable.'],
      ['Does she tell you about her day?','Yes. I am practising asking before starting mine. She should not have to wait for the forest to end.'],
      ['Nan would tell you to get to the point.','Ada does too. I appreciate an audience with standards.']),
    t('Knowing when to stop','Some days I come home empty-handed. Going farther when I am tired would not make me a better hunter.',
      ['Do you feel you have let people down?','Sometimes. Ada would rather have me home than another promise that I will be careful next time.'],
      ['What tells you it is time?','When I start stumbling or overlooking signs I would normally notice. I try to listen before I get hurt.'],
      ['It helps to hear someone admit that.','Then remember it on your own road. Coming back safely is part of the job.']),
    t('Trusting a companion’s warning','Would you stop if your dragon refused to follow you somewhere?',
      ['Yes. I would want to know why.','Good. Bramble has noticed dangers I walked straight past. His refusal deserves attention.'],
      ['I might think he was just being stubborn.','So have I. Sometimes he is. I still check before deciding that.'],
      ['We can disagree about which way to go.','Then give yourselves time to settle it. Hurrying does not make one of you right.']),
    t('Remembering the person who helped','You could have left Bramble for someone else to deal with. I have thought about that since you brought him back.',
      ['He made it very easy to like him.','He has that advantage. You still gave him your time.'],
      ['I was worried someone would be missing him.','We were. That is the part I hope you know: you ended a real worry.'],
      ['Would you have done the same for me?','Yes. I hope you never need finding, but you would not have to earn the search.']));
  p('Ada','Rowan’s wife','Ada likes a lively household, expects Rowan to listen as well as talk, and knows Bramble’s habits better than she lets on.',
    'Hello. I am Ada. If you have come looking for Rowan, say so before I offer you the wrong sort of conversation.',
    'A dragon! Rowan failed to mention that possibility when he told me to expect visitors.',
    'So you and a dragon are travelling together. I am going to need a little longer with that news than you needed to say it.',
    'Corin, welcome. You can tell me your own news before we discuss anybody else.',
    'Bramble is ours—Rowan’s hunting companion and my extremely persuasive kitchen visitor.',
    t('A disputed birthday','Rowan forgot his own birthday once. I did not correct him until he complained that everyone was being unusually nice.',
      ['Was there a celebration?','A modest one. He spent half of it trying to remember whether he had forgotten anybody else’s birthday.'],
      ['Would you want a surprise like that?','I would want warning before people expected me to enjoy a surprise.'],
      ['That sounds like something I could do.','Then accept the cake graciously. There is no need to explain how busy you were while eating it.']),
    t('A household vote','Bramble thinks a closed door is a problem the entire household ought to discuss.',
      ['Does he get his way?','Often enough to keep him hopeful, which is probably our mistake.'],
      ['What happens when you ignore him?','He finds Rowan and presents his case to a different judge.'],
      ['He sounds very determined.','He is. I admire the quality more when I am not trying to sleep.']),
    t('Keeping your own interests','I like Rowan’s stories, but I do not want every conversation I have to be about my husband.',
      ['What would you rather talk about?','I have been learning old dance steps. I enjoy discovering my feet can still surprise me.'],
      ['Does Rowan dance?','With enormous concentration and very little accuracy. He is good company anyway.'],
      ['Thank you for telling me directly.','You are welcome. It is easier than waiting for you to guess.']),
    t('Being responsible for someone','Travelling with your dragon must change how you make decisions. Does it leave much room for what you want?',
      ['We try to make decisions together.','Then keep asking each other. Familiarity can make people assume they already know the answer.'],
      ['Sometimes I worry about getting it wrong.','You will make mistakes. Admitting one promptly gives the other person a chance to help.'],
      ['Having company is something I wanted.','I am glad. Responsibility need not make the pleasure disappear.']),
    t('More than Rowan’s visitor','I am pleased you came to see me too. It is nice to become someone’s friend in my own right.',
      ['I enjoy talking with you.','Then we have a perfectly good reason for the visit. No errand required.'],
      ['Did I make you feel overlooked?','No. I was telling you something I appreciate, not asking for an apology.'],
      ['You can ask me things too.','All right: what have you enjoyed lately that has nothing to do with your responsibilities?']));
  p('Elric','Letter writer','Elric writes for neighbours who need help finding the words and treats their private news as their own.',
    'If you need help writing to someone, I can help with the words. You still get to decide what you mean.',
    'A dragon. I have written that word hundreds of times without expecting to use it as an introduction.',
    'You have a dragon companion? I promise that does not give me permission to put your news in anybody else’s letter.',
    'Hello, Corin. How are you, in words you would actually use?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. I have helped Rowan write to people; the dog makes the visits memorable.',
    t('An apology on paper','A customer asked me for an apology that did not make him sound responsible. I asked what he was apologising for.',
      ['Did he answer?','After a silence. Once he named what he had done, we could write a useful letter.'],
      ['Could you refuse the work?','Yes. But helping him say something honest seemed worth trying first.'],
      ['I find apologies difficult too.','Start with what happened and how it affected the other person. Decoration can wait.']),
    t('A letter with no reply','I can help someone write. I cannot promise that the person receiving it will answer.',
      ['Do people ask you to promise anyway?','Sometimes. Waiting makes people reach for certainty anywhere they can find it.'],
      ['Would you send another letter?','That depends on the relationship. Silence is not a puzzle I can solve without knowing the people.'],
      ['I would keep wondering whether it arrived.','Of course. It is possible to understand uncertainty and still find it miserable.']),
    t('Your own handwriting','My handwriting becomes dreadful when I write to friends. They say it is how they know I am relaxed.',
      ['Can they read it?','Usually. One friend replied to a sentence I had not intended to write at all.'],
      ['What did you do?','Agreed with her answer. It was a better conversation than the one I had planned.'],
      ['Perhaps beautiful writing is overrated.','For friendship, perhaps. Please do not tell my paying customers.']),
    t('Who gets to tell your story','People will want accounts of you and your dragon. You are allowed to keep parts of your life private.',
      ['Even if everyone is curious?','Curiosity is a reason to ask, not a right to an answer.'],
      ['I would like Nan to hear from me first.','That sounds fair. Someone who loves you should not have to piece together rumours.'],
      ['I want to tell it accurately.','Then include what you do not know. An honest gap is better than a convincing invention.']),
    t('An unsent greeting','I nearly wrote you a note, then realised I had no idea where to send it.',
      ['What would it have said?','That I hoped you were well, without demanding a magnificent account of your travels.'],
      ['You can tell me now.','I am glad you are here. There; no ink needed.'],
      ['It is nice to know I was remembered.','You were. Quiet friendships still occupy people’s thoughts.']));
  p('Mara','Baker','Mara likes bold flavours, straightforward customers, and the part of baking that gives people an excuse to gather.',
    'Hello! I am Mara. If someone has described me as the baker who argues with recipes, the description was affectionate.',
    'Well, that is a dragon. I will need a moment before I think of a greeting that fits.',
    'A dragon travelling with you? You have just made every other piece of news I heard today seem rather small.',
    'Good to see you, Corin. Have you had anything worth recommending lately?',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. I know him because he gives every baker his undivided attention.',
    t('The unpopular loaf','I made a loaf with so much pepper that nobody could agree whether it was bread or a dare.',
      ['Did you like it?','Yes. That was the awkward part. I could hardly blame everyone else for having a tongue.'],
      ['Would you make it again?','A smaller loaf, for myself. A failed crowd-pleaser can still be a private pleasure.'],
      ['I might try a little.','That is what the first person said. I admire your cautious wording.']),
    t('Borrowed recipes','I ask people where a recipe came from. “My mother” usually turns out to mean three mothers and an argument.',
      ['Does the original version matter?','It matters to the people remembering it. It need not prevent anyone cooking a different version.'],
      ['Nan never measures everything.','Then watch what she does with her hands. Some instructions have never become words.'],
      ['Have you passed one on?','Yes. Hearing someone call it their family’s favourite was unexpectedly moving.']),
    t('A quiet customer','A man bought the same small roll every week and barely spoke. When he moved away, he brought a note to thank me.',
      ['For the rolls?','For remembering which one he liked. I had not realised that mattered to him.'],
      ['Did you stay in touch?','No. It was a small part of both our lives, and still a good one.'],
      ['I would have struggled to say goodbye too.','Then I am glad he found a way that suited him. I kept the note.']),
    t('Feeding yourself as well','I hope caring for your dragon has not become another reason to forget your own meals.',
      ['I have been known to do that.','Then eat before you become too cross to recognise hunger. That is practical advice from experience.'],
      ['He would probably remind me.','Good. Let your companion look after you too.'],
      ['You sound like Nan.','I shall take that as a recommendation from someone who knows her work.']),
    t('A taste of familiarity','When you return to a place, do you hope everything will be exactly as you remember?',
      ['Some things, yes.','I understand. I like trying new recipes and knowing one familiar loaf will still be there.'],
      ['I worry that I will be the thing that changed.','You will change. People can learn who you have become without forgetting who they knew.'],
      ['I mostly hope people are pleased to see me.','Then you have had at least one successful stop today.']));
  p('Kit','Messenger','Kit carries messages around Thornwell, values clear directions, and is learning how to leave work behind at the end of the day.',
    'Kit. If you need directions, tell me the destination first. I get overenthusiastic about shortcuts.',
    'A dragon! For one wonderful moment I thought I had finally found somebody who could deliver letters faster than me.',
    'You and a dragon travel together? I promise not to turn that news into a request for a delivery.',
    'Corin! I can stop and talk. I am not late simply because I walk quickly.',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. I know the cottage, but I would check the Copper Cup while Rowan is in town.',
    t('Two people with one name','I once delivered a message to the wrong Bren. Fortunately it only asked him to return a borrowed pan.',
      ['Did he return one?','Yes. To someone who had never lent him a pan. Untangling that took longer than my route.'],
      ['How do you avoid that now?','I ask for a house or a trade as well as a name. People are less interchangeable than they sound.'],
      ['Did you admit the mistake?','I had to. There were suddenly three households arguing over cookware.']),
    t('Walking slowly','I tried taking a leisurely walk. A neighbour asked whether I had injured myself.',
      ['Did you speed up?','Immediately. Then I got annoyed with myself and slowed down again.'],
      ['Do you notice more when you go slowly?','Yes. Mostly how many people want to give a messenger one tiny extra errand.'],
      ['You could say you are off duty.','I am practising. I want to say it before I have agreed to the errand.']),
    t('Messages worth carrying','My favourite delivery was news that someone had arrived safely. Nothing dramatic; just a family getting to stop worrying.',
      ['Do you wait while they read?','Only if they need a reply sent. Their first reaction is not part of my payment.'],
      ['I should send that sort of news more often.','People appreciate it. You need not wait until you have a story worth telling.'],
      ['What is the worst sort of delivery?','One I cannot complete. I dislike leaving someone wondering whether they have been forgotten.']),
    t('A messenger’s impossible wish','I keep imagining how quickly a dragon could cross the roads I walk. Then I remember he has his own life.',
      ['Thank you for remembering that.','It is easy to turn someone impressive into a solution to your own inconvenience.'],
      ['Flying does look wonderful.','It does. I am allowed to envy the view without assigning your companion a route.'],
      ['You would miss everyone along the road.','I would. Half the job is knowing who has moved and who needs a little help.']),
    t('You can stop here','I used to think a good visit needed plenty of time. Now I am pleased when someone has five minutes they actually want to share.',
      ['I have a few minutes.','Then I shall spend them enjoying your company instead of apologising that they are few.'],
      ['Sometimes the road makes me impatient.','You can arrive in a hurry and still choose to slow down once you are here.'],
      ['I am glad you stopped rushing too.','So am I. I was in danger of becoming a very efficient person nobody knew.']));
  p('Mabel','Weaver','Mabel enjoys colour and takes pride in making clothes comfortable for the person who will actually wear them.',
    'Hello. I am Mabel. You need not pretend to know anything about weaving to talk with me.',
    'Oh my. A dragon’s wings fold so neatly. Forgive me—I am staring instead of saying hello.',
    'A dragon companion! I hope people ask about him with better manners than I am managing just now.',
    'Corin, welcome back. What has caught your eye lately?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. I once mended a coat that the dog had enthusiastically helped him wear out.',
    t('Choosing a colour','A customer asked for a sensible colour, then looked miserable at every sensible colour I suggested.',
      ['What did they really want?','Bright yellow. We eventually established that nobody had forbidden them to enjoy yellow.'],
      ['Is it harder to keep clean?','Sometimes. They decided they would rather wash a coat they liked than resent a practical one.'],
      ['I do that with things I want.','Then ask yourself whose disapproval you are expecting. It may be somebody who never gets a vote.']),
    t('The itchy masterpiece','I made a beautiful scarf from wool that itched dreadfully. Compliments did not improve it.',
      ['What happened to it?','It became decoration. I refused to make someone wear my pride around their neck.'],
      ['Was it hard to admit the problem?','Very. I had spent far longer on it than on plenty of useful things.'],
      ['What do you check first now?','How the cloth feels. The person wearing it will live with that long after the first compliment.']),
    t('A pattern from memory','I can remember the pattern on my mother’s sleeves more clearly than the sound of her laugh. I wish it were the other way round.',
      ['Have you made that pattern yourself?','Yes. It brought back the feeling of holding her hand, which I had not expected.'],
      ['I wish I remembered more about my parents.','I am sorry, Corin. Wanting more does not mean the memories you do have are inadequate.'],
      ['Would you tell me what she was like?','Patient until people mistook patience for agreement. Then she became wonderfully specific.']),
    t('A dragon’s colours','When you describe your companion, do you begin with what he looks like or what he is like?',
      ['Usually I try to explain that he is my friend.','That tells me more about your life than a list of colours would.'],
      ['People tend to ask about his wings first.','I nearly did too. Beautiful things can distract us from introducing ourselves properly.'],
      ['I still enjoy how extraordinary he looks.','Of course. Affection does not require you to stop noticing beauty.']),
    t('Being recognised','I was pleased to recognise you coming back. There is comfort in having another familiar person in the world.',
      ['I feel that when I reach Thornwell.','Then the town is becoming more than a mark along your route.'],
      ['Even if I cannot stay long?','A short visit can still tell someone they have not been forgotten.'],
      ['I wanted to hear how you were doing.','Well, thank you. I have finally chosen a colour for something of my own. It is gloriously impractical.']));
  p('Bren','Amateur historian','Bren likes finding out how ordinary decisions become the events people later call history.',
    'Hello. Are you visiting the school? I am quite capable of discussing something else, but I like to establish the opportunity.',
    'A dragon, here in my lifetime. I had imagined that sentence belonging to somebody in a history book.',
    'You are travelling with a dragon? Then the histories I read have failed to prepare me for a perfectly ordinary introduction.',
    'Corin. What have you been wondering about?',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. This is one identification for which I do not need to consult a book.',
    t('The person who cooked supper','I am interested in who fed a travelling army. Histories count soldiers carefully and become vague about everyone carrying the food.',
      ['Why does that interest you?','Because a journey depends on work that rarely gets a name. I want to know whose work it was.'],
      ['Can you find out?','Sometimes from household accounts. Not every question has survived with an answer.'],
      ['Nan would ask who washed up afterwards.','A very good question. She would improve several histories I have read.']),
    t('An argument I lost','I argued about a date until Elowen showed me I had confused two people with the same name.',
      ['Did you apologise?','Yes, though I began by explaining how understandable the mistake was. She waited for the actual apology.'],
      ['Was the rest of your argument wrong?','Enough of it that I had to begin again. I enjoyed the second attempt less and trusted it more.'],
      ['I would have wanted to disappear.','So did I. Staying to listen turned out to be less painful than imagining everyone discussing it later.']),
    t('Remembering an ordinary day','If somebody wrote about your childhood, what small thing would you want included?',
      ['The way Nan called me in for supper.','Yes. A life described only by its crises would leave that voice out.'],
      ['I am not sure my childhood needs a book.','It does not. I was asking what matters to you, not offering a commission.'],
      ['Probably something funny and embarrassing.','Then you would be doing future readers a kindness. Solemn people become difficult company after enough pages.']),
    t('A living account','Would you mind if I asked about travelling with a dragon? You can decline anything personal.',
      ['Ask about what the journey feels like.','All right. Is having company comforting even when you disagree about the road?'],
      ['I do not want every visit to be an interview.','Fair. I can be interested in you without collecting material.'],
      ['I am still making sense of it myself.','Then an unfinished answer would be entirely appropriate. Experience does not arrive already explained.']),
    t('A visitor, not a source','I caught myself preparing questions before you returned. Then I remembered you might simply want a friendly conversation.',
      ['I would like that today.','Then tell me whether you have eaten anything good. I shall resist asking for dates and witnesses.'],
      ['I do like your questions sometimes.','Thank you. I will try to leave room for the times you do not.'],
      ['What has happened to you since we spoke?','I lent out a favourite book and managed not to ask for it back immediately. A modest triumph.']));
  p('Berta','Retired herbalist','Berta still prepares stock for Wren and is discovering interests that do not involve being needed by a customer.',
    'If you came for the stall, Wren runs it now. If you came for a conversation, you have the correct person.',
    'That is a dragon. I am old enough to have imagined this and sensible enough to be startled anyway.',
    'A dragon chose to travel with you? I hope you have someone you can admit your worries to.',
    'Come to talk, Corin? Good. I was in danger of having an entire conversation with my own opinions.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. The dog has never understood why medicinal herbs smell interesting but make disappointing snacks.',
    t('Advice nobody asked for','I have discovered that retirement gives me more advice than anyone needs to hear.',
      ['How do you know when to offer it?','I ask whether someone wants an opinion. A revolutionary technique I could have learned forty years earlier.'],
      ['Does Wren tell you to stop?','Clearly and kindly. I taught her to be precise, and now I suffer the consequences.'],
      ['I could use some advice sometimes.','Then ask. I will try to answer the question you bring instead of the one I prefer.']),
    t('A beginner again','I have taken to sketching birds. At present, every bird resembles a disappointed potato.',
      ['Are you enjoying it?','Very much, when I remember I am allowed to be bad at it.'],
      ['Would you show someone?','Wren has seen them. She identified one as a bird, which was encouragingly specific.'],
      ['What will you draw next?','Another bird. I refuse to let potatoes win this easily.']),
    t('Work you cannot finish','There is always another person who needs help. I used to treat that as a reason never to rest.',
      ['What changed?','I became too tired to listen properly. Wren noticed before I admitted it.'],
      ['Did you feel guilty stopping?','Yes. Feeling guilty did not prove I was doing the wrong thing.'],
      ['I worry about that on the road.','Then let other people help where they can. You are a person, not an inexhaustible supply.']),
    t('Looking after the carer','Who notices when caring for your dragon has worn you out?',
      ['He notices more than I expect.','Then believe him when he asks you to rest. Care should be allowed to travel both ways.'],
      ['I try not to let anyone see.','That sounds lonely. You need not earn company by appearing easy to look after.'],
      ['I am learning to notice it myself.','Good. It is easier to choose a rest than recover after your body chooses one for you.']),
    t('A better drawing','My latest bird actually looks like the species I intended. I am trying not to announce this to everyone.',
      ['You can announce it to me.','A robin. Two feet, one beak, and an expression that is almost intentional.'],
      ['You sound delighted.','I am. It is pleasant to improve at something nobody depends on.'],
      ['Will you keep the first drawings?','Yes. They will remind me that enjoying myself began before getting good.']));
  p('Della','Gardener','Della likes patient work and dislikes being told that a small interest needs a grand purpose.',
    'Hello. I am Della. I hope you have come with a story, because my news mostly concerns slugs.',
    'A dragon! I thought a fox in my garden was going to remain my most surprising visitor.',
    'You have a dragon for company? I would need time to stop being astonished and start being useful.',
    'Corin. I promise there are subjects available besides gardening.',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. He once dug up something I had spent all morning planting, then looked pleased to have helped.',
    t('Growing something useless','I grew flowers nobody could eat, sell, or use as medicine. A neighbour asked what they were for.',
      ['What did you tell them?','That I liked looking at them. It took me a moment to realise that was a complete answer.'],
      ['Did the neighbour like them?','Eventually. I suspect enjoying something without an excuse took practice.'],
      ['I like finding flowers on the road.','Then they are doing the same job there. You need not carry them away to keep the pleasure.']),
    t('A terrible bargain','I agreed to trade gardening help with a neighbour. We both chose the jobs we most disliked and discovered they were the same jobs.',
      ['What did you do?','Worked together and complained. The work was not better, but the afternoon was.'],
      ['Did you keep the arrangement?','Yes. Company turned out to be the useful part of the bargain.'],
      ['I would have tried to escape the agreement.','I considered pretending to be ill. My neighbour arrived looking equally tempted.']),
    t('Leaving room for mistakes','I used to pull up anything I had not planted. Then I learned how many seedlings I had simply forgotten about.',
      ['How do you decide now?','I wait until I can recognise them. Untidiness for a week is cheaper than losing a whole crop.'],
      ['Does waiting bother you?','Immensely. Patience is not my natural expression; it is something I practise.'],
      ['I like knowing you do not get everything right.','Then you are going to find me excellent company.']),
    t('A creature with preferences','I expect people have a great many suggestions about what your dragon ought to be like.',
      ['They often expect him to be frightening.','That must make an ordinary introduction hard work for both of you.'],
      ['I am still learning what he likes.','Then let him surprise you. Familiarity should make room for new discoveries.'],
      ['Some suggestions are helpful.','Keep those. You do not have to reject kindness just because it comes with an imperfect guess.']),
    t('A visit that can be quiet','You seem to spend a lot of time answering questions. We can have a quiet conversation if you prefer.',
      ['Quiet sounds good.','Then there is no hurry. I am pleased you are here.'],
      ['I would rather hear about your week.','A seed I thought had failed finally sprouted. That was quite enough excitement for one morning.'],
      ['I am happy to talk today.','Good. Tell me something you enjoyed, before we get to anything you had to endure.']));
  p('Ewan','Student of local history','Ewan wants to understand how stories change when different people remember the same event.',
    'Hello. I am Ewan. If you enjoy a question with more than one answer, we should get along.',
    'There is a dragon beside you. I had several clever questions ready, and every one of them has vanished.',
    'Travelling with a dragon must give you a different perspective on all our arguments about them.',
    'Corin, hello. You do not have to bring me news; your company will do.',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. The dog is rather better known than many people who live here.',
    t('Two versions of a festival','I asked two neighbours about the same festival. One remembered wonderful music; the other remembered losing a shoe.',
      ['Could both accounts be right?','Of course. I had been asking what happened without asking what happened to them.'],
      ['Did the shoe turn up?','Yes. The owner considered that the conclusion of the story. The musician barely mentioned it.'],
      ['Which version did you write down?','Both, with the speakers’ names. I should not make them agree just to tidy my notes.']),
    t('Reading something ridiculous','I enjoy badly exaggerated adventures. It is a relief to read a story whose author has no interest in being believed.',
      ['How exaggerated?','A hero once crossed a river by politely asking the fish to hold still.'],
      ['Does that spoil serious books for you?','No. It reminds me that reading can be for pleasure as well as for proving something.'],
      ['I would like that sort of help on the road.','I suspect real fish would have scheduling objections.']),
    t('Changing your mind in public','I find it easier to change my mind privately than to tell someone who heard my first opinion.',
      ['Why is the second part harder?','Because I want credit for learning without admitting I needed to learn. It is not my finest quality.'],
      ['Would you judge someone else for changing theirs?','Usually I would be pleased. I ought to offer myself the same courtesy.'],
      ['You are admitting it now.','Yes. Apparently knowing the problem is a beginning rather than a cure.']),
    t('A story your companion would tell','Do you think your dragon would describe your journey the same way you would?',
      ['Probably not every part of it.','I would like that. Two accounts can reveal more than one very confident account.'],
      ['He would mention my mistakes.','Then perhaps agree that each of you gets to mention one of your own first.'],
      ['Some parts would matter more to him.','That is what interests me. Sharing a road does not mean experiencing the same journey.']),
    t('Asking a smaller question','I was going to ask what you have learned on your travels. That is rather a large demand for a greeting.',
      ['Ask what surprised me most recently.','All right. I like a question that leaves room for a small answer.'],
      ['I might not know until later.','Fair. We can talk about the experience before deciding what it means.'],
      ['You can just ask whether I am well.','Are you well, Corin? I would like the honest answer.']));
  p('Osric','Weaver and reader','Osric combines a working knowledge of cloth with an enthusiasm for stories that do not always behave themselves.',
    'Hello. I am Osric. You can interrupt my thoughts; they were going round in circles anyway.',
    'A dragon. That rather settles whether my day was going to be ordinary.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I will try not to make you repeat that merely because I enjoy hearing it.',
    'Corin, good to see you. Has anything made you laugh today?',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. I recognise him more reliably than I recognise Rowan’s latest coat.',
    t('Cloth for a child','A parent once asked me to make a child’s coat with room to grow. The child asked for room to climb.',
      ['Could you do both?','Yes, once I heard the second request. The person wearing it had useful information.'],
      ['Was the parent annoyed?','Briefly, then amused. We had all forgotten the child could answer questions.'],
      ['Did the coat survive?','Longer than expected. I considered the grass stains evidence that it was doing its job.']),
    t('A story with a bad ending','I once read a story in which the hero woke up and none of it had happened. I felt I had been tricked into worrying.',
      ['Could that ending ever work?','Perhaps, if the waking mattered as much as the dream. This one merely saved the author some trouble.'],
      ['Would you change it?','In my head, repeatedly. I have spent more time fixing that story than reading it.'],
      ['What ending did you want?','One where the people who helped were remembered. They had done rather a lot of work.']),
    t('A useful interruption','I dislike being interrupted until I have been left alone too long. Then I become offended that nobody visits.',
      ['That seems difficult for your friends.','They have learned to ask whether I want company and ignore any theatrical sighing.'],
      ['Should I come back later?','No. I was confessing a fault, not performing it. Stay and talk.'],
      ['I sometimes want both things too.','Then we can be slightly contradictory people together.']),
    t('A hero’s ordinary afternoon','Do people expect every day with your dragon to be an adventure?',
      ['Some days I just want things to go smoothly.','That sounds like an excellent afternoon. Stories rarely give enough credit to a comfortable day.'],
      ['There are ordinary moments too.','Good. I would hate for your whole life to become something exhausting to describe.'],
      ['I still find the ordinary moments remarkable.','Then perhaps you have the better story after all.']),
    t('Someone to be ordinary with','You do not have to be impressive here. I have enough impressive characters in books.',
      ['I could tell you about a mistake.','Only if you find it funny now. I am offering company, not requesting an embarrassment.'],
      ['What if I have done something impressive?','Then I reserve the right to be delighted. I said it was not a requirement.'],
      ['That is a comfortable sort of welcome.','Good. I would like to get better at those.']));
  p('Alder','Beekeeper','Alder keeps bees, enjoys a practical experiment, and knows when enthusiasm has become too much information.',
    'Hello. I am Alder. If you ask about bees, I may need help knowing when to stop.',
    'That is a dragon! I understand bees well enough to stay calm around them. Dragons will take more practice.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then you have a companion whose habits are more interesting than most people’s opinions about him.',
    'Corin, welcome. I can offer a conversation with only a reasonable number of bees in it.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. He has had the good sense to leave my bees alone.',
    t('A swarm in the wrong place','A swarm settled where nobody wanted it. Everyone wanted me to hurry; hurrying would only have made the bees harder to move.',
      ['Did people listen?','After I explained what I was doing. Being told to wait is easier when you know why.'],
      ['Were you frightened?','A little. Familiar work can still go wrong if I stop paying attention.'],
      ['Did you move them safely?','Yes. The least dramatic outcome took the most preparation.']),
    t('The taste of a season','Honey changes with the flowers the bees visit. People sometimes complain that this year does not taste like last year.',
      ['Can you make it taste the same?','Not honestly. I can explain the difference and let them decide whether they like it.'],
      ['Do you have a favourite?','The first honey after a difficult winter. Relief has a powerful influence on taste.'],
      ['I think I would enjoy the differences.','Then you would be a pleasant customer to talk with.']),
    t('Gwyneth’s limit','Gwyneth once asked for an answer without the history of beekeeping attached. I am still practising.',
      ['Can you manage a short answer?','Yes. There. A triumph.'],
      ['Does she enjoy hearing about your work?','She does. Enjoying something does not mean wanting it to fill every meal.'],
      ['I like hearing someone care about a subject.','Thank you. I will try to remember you can also care about several other subjects.']),
    t('Not every creature needs taming','I hope people do not keep asking how you made your dragon obey.',
      ['They misunderstand our friendship.','Then I am sorry. Working with a living creature should begin by noticing what it wants.'],
      ['How do you explain your bees?','That I manage the conditions, not every bee. It is less grand and much more accurate.'],
      ['Sometimes cooperation is difficult.','Yes. Respect does not make disagreement vanish; it changes how you handle it.']),
    t('A shorter answer','I remembered your visit while telling someone about my work. I stopped long enough to ask about theirs.',
      ['What did you learn?','That they restore old shoes. I had known them for years and somehow missed that.'],
      ['Did they appreciate being asked?','Very much. Apparently I had been providing an excellent audience with no opportunities to speak.'],
      ['You can ask about me now.','What would you like to do next, if nobody else needed anything from you for an afternoon?']));
  p('Gwyneth','Thornwell neighbour','Gwyneth likes clear invitations, lively company, and ensuring quiet people get to finish their sentences.',
    'Hello. I am Gwyneth. Do you want advice, directions, or simply somebody to talk to?',
    'Oh! A dragon. Give me a moment to stop staring; I would like to welcome him with some dignity.',
    'You have a dragon companion? I hope you are enjoying his company as well as worrying about keeping him safe.',
    'Corin, it is good to hear your voice again.',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. Ada pretends to be sterner with him than Rowan is; I am unconvinced.',
    t('An invitation people can refuse','I used to say “You must come” when I meant “I would enjoy your company.” They are not quite the same invitation.',
      ['What changed your mind?','A friend came while exhausted because she thought I would be hurt. I had wanted to give her a pleasant evening.'],
      ['Do people still visit?','Yes. Now I can believe they wanted to.'],
      ['I find refusing difficult.','Then practise a small refusal with someone kind. You need not begin with the most difficult person you know.']),
    t('Sharing a conversation','Alder and I sometimes tell the same story differently. We have learned not to correct every detail while the other is speaking.',
      ['What if the detail matters?','Then we add it afterwards. Most details are not emergencies.'],
      ['Who tells it better?','Depends which of us you ask. I would recommend asking me.'],
      ['Do you ever forget whose story it was?','Frequently. That is what happens when you have shared enough afternoons.']),
    t('A song you cannot finish','I remember the first line of a childhood song and none of the rest. Every suggested ending sounds wrong.',
      ['Could you make up a new ending?','I could. I think I am really hoping to hear my sister sing it again.'],
      ['Does your sister remember?','No, and she insists my first line is wrong too. We have made no progress at all.'],
      ['It still sounds like a good memory.','It is. An incomplete memory can still make me happy.']),
    t('Two different sorts of tired','Does your dragon notice when you are worried, even if you are not physically tired?',
      ['He is getting better at it.','Then let him know when he is right. Guessing constantly would be tiring for him too.'],
      ['Sometimes I need to explain.','That is fair. Caring about someone does not make them able to read every expression.'],
      ['I do not always want to talk about it.','You can say that kindly. Quiet company is still company.']),
    t('An honest answer is welcome','When I ask how you are, I am not requiring a cheerful answer.',
      ['I am glad. Some days are difficult.','Then we can acknowledge that without pretending I can mend everything in one conversation.'],
      ['Today I really am glad to be here.','Then I shall enjoy hearing it without searching for a hidden worry.'],
      ['How are you, Gwyneth?','Pleased you asked. I have had a rather ordinary week, and that has suited me.']));
  p('Archivist Elowen','School archivist','Elowen helps readers find reliable accounts and insists that uncertainty be recorded as carefully as a fact.',
    'Welcome to the school. I am Elowen. Are you looking for a particular subject, or would you like help choosing one?',
    'A dragon. Please give me a moment: I have spent years explaining why a picture cannot settle what a living one is like.',
    'You are travelling with a dragon? Thank you for telling me yourself. I will not treat that confidence as a public announcement.',
    'Hello, Corin. What would you like to make sense of today?',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. The dog is a familiar visitor around the school grounds.',
    t('A book with the answer missing','A reader once accused me of lending an incomplete book because it did not answer his question. The last page was present; the knowledge simply was not.',
      ['Was he angry with you?','At first. Then we looked for other accounts. Anger was easier for him than admitting he felt lost.'],
      ['How can you tell a book is wrong?','Compare it with independent evidence and ask how its author knew. A confident voice is not evidence.'],
      ['That would frustrate me too.','Me as well. Wanting an answer does not oblige the world to have preserved one.']),
    t('A reader who struggled','A grown man once whispered that he read slowly. He thought the school would only welcome him if he could hide it.',
      ['What did you say?','That he could take his time. Then I made sure my behaviour agreed with my words.'],
      ['Did he keep visiting?','Yes. I will leave the rest of his story to him; he did not come here to become an example.'],
      ['Could someone ask you for help quietly?','Of course. Learning need not begin with an audience.']),
    t('How a king edits the past','An official account can make a decision look inevitable by leaving out everybody who opposed it.',
      ['Does that happen in accounts of Wingfall?','Yes. Halvard’s preferred histories treat his victory as proof that nobody else had a valid claim.'],
      ['How do you teach around that?','By naming who wrote each account and comparing what they omit. Students deserve to see the method.'],
      ['Do you ever worry about keeping those books?','I do. Being frightened is one reason to be careful, not a reason to tell students a falsehood.']),
    t('The difference between dragons','I hope people do not judge your companion entirely by what they know of Halvard’s mount.',
      ['Some people are frightened before we speak.','Give them time where you can. Fear learned over years rarely disappears during one introduction.'],
      ['He deserves to speak for himself.','Agreed. If he wants you to convey something, I would listen without pretending I had heard his voice myself.'],
      ['I have questions about the older riders.','Ask. I will distinguish the records we have from the conclusions I draw from them.']),
    t('What the next account should include','If you ever describe this journey for someone else, include the people who helped you get through an ordinary day.',
      ['I would include this school.','I would be glad of that. Include a question we could not answer as well as anything useful we supplied.'],
      ['Would anyone want to read the ordinary parts?','They may be the parts that make another traveller feel less alone.'],
      ['I am not ready to turn it into a story.','Then do not. Living through an event and explaining it are different tasks.']));
  p('Mira','Student of mining history','Mira studies work underground and wants advice about dangerous places to be useful to the people entering them.',
    'Hello, I am Mira. Are you headed towards the mining towns? I have been studying accounts from the workings.',
    'A dragon! I did not expect the most surprising thing I learned today to walk up without a book.',
    'Your companion is a dragon? I would like to hear about him, provided you are not tired of explaining yourself.',
    'Corin, hello. Did you come for information or company?',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. I recognise him from the paths around the school.',
    t('What a miner’s note leaves out','A mining account said a passage was “easy.” It was written by someone who had used it for twenty years.',
      ['Easy for them, perhaps.','Exactly. A visitor needs to know about footing and turns, not how familiar the author felt.'],
      ['Can you make the advice more useful?','I compare accounts and describe the actual obstacles. I mark anything I have not verified.'],
      ['Have you been underground yourself?','Not into the dangerous workings. That is a limitation I should state before offering advice.']),
    t('The question that stopped a lesson','I asked what happens to a miner’s family after an accident. We had spent an hour discussing how much ore a mine produced.',
      ['Did the teacher answer?','She found a family account for the next lesson. I appreciated that she did not pretend to know immediately.'],
      ['Were other students interested?','Yes. Some had relatives in mining towns. I should have thought to ask them earlier.'],
      ['That seems more important than the ore.','Both belong in the account. A mine does not produce anything without people doing the work.']),
    t('A map I can read','I copied a beautiful map and made the labels too small to read without leaning over it.',
      ['Was it for an assignment?','Yes. My teacher praised the care and asked whether I had tried using it.'],
      ['Did you redraw it?','I did. It looked less elegant and worked considerably better.'],
      ['I would rather find the way than admire the lettering.','So would I when lost. I am trying to remember that while comfortably seated.']),
    t('Places wings cannot help','Does travelling with your dragon make it harder to enter a place where you cannot stay together?',
      ['I worry when we have to separate.','That makes sense. Knowing where you will meet would not remove every worry, but it gives you a plan.'],
      ['We decide what is worth the risk.','I am glad you decide together. An impressive ability does not make every route sensible.'],
      ['I try to prepare for what I can handle alone.','Good. A companion can help without becoming your only plan.']),
    t('Useful news from the road','I am learning to ask travellers what advice was missing, instead of only asking whether our advice was correct.',
      ['Knowing when to turn back matters.','Yes. A route description should not make retreat sound like failure.'],
      ['Sometimes people need practical details.','Where to rest, what supplies to bring, what signs to watch. Those deserve space on the page.'],
      ['You could ask how frightened they were.','I should. Advice written as if nobody feels fear can be hard to use when you do.']));
  p('Oren','Student of spirits','Oren studies accounts of the dead while trying to remember that frightening stories often began with somebody’s grief.',
    'I am Oren. I study accounts of spirits. You may ask why, but please let me finish before deciding I am peculiar.',
    'A dragon! I spend so much time reading about things people cannot see that I was not prepared for this.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would like to know more, but I promise not to begin with a dreadful prediction.',
    'Hello, Corin. I have been practising beginning conversations with something cheerful.',
    'That dog is Bramble, Rowan’s companion. He is entirely alive and very pleased about it.',
    t('Why study frightening things?','I grew up hearing frightening stories without any explanation of what people had actually witnessed. I wanted to separate the two.',
      ['Did the research make you less frightened?','Of some things. Better informed is not always the same as less frightened.'],
      ['Do you enjoy a scary story anyway?','Yes, when everyone knows it is a story. I dislike fear being passed off as instruction.'],
      ['What if an account has no explanation?','I leave it unresolved. An unanswered question is better than an answer made to sound certain.']),
    t('A memorial without a name','I read about a memorial whose name had worn away. People still left flowers there.',
      ['Why, if they did not know who it was?','Some had made it a place to remember their own dead. The missing name had not made it meaningless.'],
      ['Did anyone try to find the name?','Yes. I hope they succeed, though I would not want their search to dismiss the people already visiting.'],
      ['I sometimes struggle to remember my parents.','I am sorry. Remembering can include what others tell you; it need not be a test you pass alone.']),
    t('Choosing when to tell a story','I once described a haunting during supper. I had mistaken everyone going quiet for everyone being interested.',
      ['What happened?','Someone asked whether I could let them finish eating before explaining what had happened to the cook.'],
      ['Was the story true?','That was not the urgent problem, as my host made clear.'],
      ['Do you ask first now?','Yes. An audience should be allowed to keep its appetite.']),
    t('What companionship changes','People imagine a dragon makes someone fearless. I imagine it gives you someone else to worry about.',
      ['That is much closer to it.','Then I hope there are people who ask how you both are, instead of simply admiring your courage.'],
      ['He also helps me feel safe.','Both can be true. Loving company can comfort you and give you something precious to lose.'],
      ['I do not want to spend every day worrying.','Of course. Enjoying the company matters too; it is why the worry means anything.']),
    t('Something cheerful, as promised','I finally found a spirit story in which nobody is punished, frightened, or warned away.',
      ['What does the spirit do?','It helps a lost traveller find a familiar path. I wish more storytellers thought that was worth remembering.'],
      ['Do you believe it happened?','I cannot establish that. I can still be pleased someone chose to tell a kind story.'],
      ['That was a good choice for today.','I thought so. I am learning that timing is part of being good company.']));
  p('Tamsin','Student and reader','Tamsin reads widely, questions frightening rumours, and enjoys stories whose characters have ordinary wants.',
    'Hello. I am Tamsin. Are you here to study, or hiding from an errand? I will not insist on knowing which.',
    'A dragon! Please tell me I am allowed to be excited before I work out how to behave.',
    'You have a dragon companion? I would like to hear his actual story before repeating anyone else’s version.',
    'Corin, hello. Have you found time to enjoy anything lately?',
    'That is Rowan’s dog, Bramble. He is much less mysterious than people make the woods sound.',
    t('A villain who wanted lunch','My favourite part of an adventure was the villain stopping to eat. For one page he seemed like a person who had to organise a day.',
      ['Did it make him less frightening?','No. It made him more believable. Frightening people do ordinary things too.'],
      ['Perhaps you were just hungry.','Also possible. I try to allow more than one explanation for my opinions.'],
      ['Would you write that kind of story?','I might. First I would need to decide what happened after lunch.']),
    t('A rumour about a witch','People tell elaborate stories about Maelis in Witchmoor. I am interested in how few of the storytellers have spoken to her.',
      ['Could the stories still be true?','Some details could be. Repeating them does not improve the evidence.'],
      ['Would you visit her yourself?','Not without preparing for the road. Doubting a rumour does not make the journey harmless.'],
      ['I would rather make up my own mind.','Then ask her questions and listen. An introduction is a better start than an accusation.']),
    t('Writing the first sentence','I keep planning a story so thoroughly that I never begin writing it.',
      ['What stops you?','As long as it stays in my head, it can still be perfect. The first sentence has to be actual words.'],
      ['Could you begin in the middle?','That might work. I know the argument I want two characters to have better than I know the weather.'],
      ['Would it help to tell it aloud?','Perhaps. An interested listener might keep me from revising the same sentence forever.']),
    t('The story strangers expect','Do strangers expect you and your dragon to behave like characters from a tale?',
      ['They sometimes expect me to know exactly what to do.','That sounds exhausting. Most stories remove the hours people spent deciding.'],
      ['Some just want a good look at him.','I understand the curiosity. I hope they ask before making him uncomfortable.'],
      ['I expected things to be different too.','Then you are allowed to learn your way into the real version.']),
    t('I wrote the first page','I finally began my story. The first page is untidy, and I am surprisingly fond of it.',
      ['What helped you begin?','I let the characters argue before explaining the entire world. They had more to say than the landscape.'],
      ['Will you let someone read it?','When I am ready. I want to finish something before collecting everyone’s preferred version.'],
      ['I am glad you told me.','I wanted to. Sharing a small piece of good news makes it feel more settled.']));
  p('Master Iven','Schoolteacher','Iven wants students to understand how to reach an answer and to feel safe asking the question that comes before it.',
    'Welcome. I am Iven. You need not be enrolled here to ask a question.',
    'A dragon. I suspect my students would enjoy seeing their teacher completely at a loss for words.',
    'A dragon travels with you? Then I should begin by asking what you have learned, not by delivering a lecture.',
    'Corin. I hope your questions are getting more interesting, even if the answers remain difficult.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. He is a cheerful visitor with very little regard for a lesson’s duration.',
    t('The question before the lesson','A pupil once asked why we should believe the map. It delayed my lesson and improved it considerably.',
      ['What did you tell them?','That a map is somebody’s account of a place. We should ask who made it, when, and for what purpose.'],
      ['Did you mind being interrupted?','For an instant. Teachers are people, including the inconvenient parts.'],
      ['Would you trust a traveller more?','I would ask the traveller the same questions. Recent experience can be useful and still incomplete.']),
    t('A lesson taught badly','I once answered a hesitant question too quickly. The pupil stopped asking questions, and I mistook that for understanding.',
      ['How did you find out?','I asked privately. Then I had to listen without explaining why I had meant well.'],
      ['Did you apologise?','Yes. A teacher who cannot admit an error teaches a very unhelpful lesson.'],
      ['I sometimes pretend to understand.','You are welcome to say that here. We can start from where you actually are.']),
    t('Learning without a prize','I enjoy studying things I will never be particularly good at. It reminds me that interest is a reason in itself.',
      ['What are you learning?','Bird calls. At present I can confidently identify a crow and several noises that are not a crow.'],
      ['Do your students know?','Yes. They enjoy correcting me, which is fair compensation for my profession.'],
      ['I like being good at something.','So do I. I simply do not want that to become the only reason I try.']),
    t('Who teaches the rider?','Who helps you think through a decision about travelling with your dragon?',
      ['We talk things through together.','Good. Advice from outside can help, but the two of you live with the result.'],
      ['I ask people who know more than I do.','Ask how they know. Expertise in one thing can disguise uncertainty in another.'],
      ['Sometimes I have to decide before I feel ready.','Then choose with the information you have, and allow yourself to revise when you learn more.']),
    t('You are allowed to come back','People sometimes think returning to ask for help means they learned nothing the first time.',
      ['I have worried about that.','A new situation can expose a new question. Learning does not end when you leave the room.'],
      ['Would you ever get tired of my questions?','I might get tired. That is when I should rest, not convince you curiosity is a fault.'],
      ['I came to visit rather than ask for help.','Then I am doubly pleased: you know you can ask, and you chose company today.']));
  p('Brin','Student of rider temples','Brin studies the three elemental temples and is learning to describe dangerous places without turning them into invitations to be reckless.',
    'Hello, I am Brin. I study the old temples. If you have come for directions, I will keep the history until afterwards.',
    'A dragon! I have been studying places built for riders, and now I cannot think how to introduce myself to one.',
    'Your companion is a dragon? Then the temples may matter to you in a way a classroom cannot reproduce.',
    'Corin, good to see you. What would be useful to know?',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. Returning a dog is a much more manageable expedition than most of the ones I read about.',
    t('A door drawn too small','I copied a temple plan without checking its scale. My version would have required every ancient rider to crawl.',
      ['Did anyone notice before you handed it in?','Iven asked where I would put the door handle. I understood the problem rather quickly.'],
      ['How did you correct it?','I checked the measurements instead of enlarging whatever looked wrong. Guessing had caused enough trouble.'],
      ['Were you embarrassed?','Very. Now it is one of the few mistakes I can explain without flinching.']),
    t('Why preserve a ruin?','A ruined place can still tell us how people lived. Rebuilding it according to our guesses can erase the evidence.',
      ['Would you leave everything untouched?','Not if it were falling on people. Preserving evidence should not mean ignoring danger.'],
      ['What interests you besides the grand halls?','Wear on a step. A repair. Something that proves the place was used rather than merely admired.'],
      ['I would want to imagine it whole.','So would I. I just want to know when I am imagining.']),
    t('The expedition I am not ready for','I would like to visit the temples. Wanting to go does not yet make me prepared for what is inside.',
      ['What would you need first?','Companions, supplies, and a much more honest assessment of my ability to handle danger.'],
      ['Does waiting frustrate you?','Yes. I am trying to make preparation more than a polite word for daydreaming.'],
      ['You can still do useful work here.','I can. Thank you for not making that sound like a consolation prize.']),
    t('Old buildings, living companions','I keep reminding myself that your dragon is not here to confirm everything I have read.',
      ['He would have his own questions.','I would like to hear them, if he wants to share. Our ignorance may overlap in interesting ways.'],
      ['Some of the books might be wrong.','Then I would rather discover it than protect a favourite theory.'],
      ['You can ask without expecting certainty.','Thank you. “I do not know” should be a possible answer on both sides.']),
    t('After the first Heartstone','The Lightning Heartstone is no longer only something you were looking for. How are you feeling about that?',
      ['Pleased, but aware of how much remains.','That seems fair. Reaching one goal can reveal the size of the next without making the first less real.'],
      ['I want a rest before thinking about the next temple.','Then take one. A list of destinations is not an order to leave immediately.'],
      ['I wish the books had prepared us for everything.','So do I. If you choose to tell us what was missing, I will listen carefully.']));
  p('Nell','History student','Nell questions official language and enjoys catching an argument that has quietly changed the subject.',
    'I am Nell. If you have come to ask where something is, I promise not to turn it into a debate.',
    'A dragon! I was about to say I had heard every possible distraction from studying. I retract that claim.',
    'You travel with a dragon? That makes some of the confident things people say about dragons sound rather premature.',
    'Hello, Corin. I have a question, but you may finish arriving first.',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. There is no academic dispute about that, whatever else this school argues over.',
    t('The word “necessary”','When a royal history calls something necessary, I ask necessary for whom. It often means necessary for the king to keep what he wanted.',
      ['Does that change how you read it?','Yes. It makes me look for the people who paid the price of that decision.'],
      ['Could the decision still have been necessary?','Possibly. Then the author should be able to explain why, instead of using the word as the explanation.'],
      ['Do people get annoyed with your questions?','Sometimes. Annoyance is not an answer, though I am learning not to say that quite so triumphantly.']),
    t('Winning an argument badly','I once won an argument by pointing out a friend’s mistake in front of everyone. She stopped discussing the subject with me.',
      ['Did you talk to her afterwards?','Yes. I had to apologise for how I treated her without demanding she admit I was right.'],
      ['Were you actually right?','About the fact, yes. That did not settle whether I had behaved well.'],
      ['I would have wanted to show everyone too.','So did I. I am trying to notice that impulse before it becomes the point of the conversation.']),
    t('A question for pleasure','I like debating which meal is best after a long walk. Nobody has to win, and the evidence is enjoyable.',
      ['Bread while it is still warm.','A persuasive opening. I would ask what you put on it, but I might become hungry enough to abandon the discussion.'],
      ['Anything Nan has made.','You have introduced an emotional advantage I cannot reasonably challenge.'],
      ['Whatever I packed before leaving.','Practical. Your argument is available precisely when required.']),
    t('What the crown calls a threat','Halvard treats another dragon as a threat to his authority. That does not tell us what your companion wants.',
      ['He wants to live his own life.','Then that belongs in the discussion before the king’s fears do.'],
      ['We still have to take the danger seriously.','Yes. Understanding an accusation is unfair does not stop someone powerful acting on it.'],
      ['I am tired of other people deciding who we are.','I can understand that. I will ask you, and accept that you do not owe every question an answer.']),
    t('An argument I put aside','A friend and I disagreed, and this time I managed to enjoy the rest of the afternoon anyway.',
      ['That sounds like progress.','It felt suspiciously like losing for the first few minutes. Then it felt rather pleasant.'],
      ['Did you settle the disagreement?','No. We discovered we could still choose supper without resolving the entire subject.'],
      ['Would you manage that with me?','I would try. I like talking with you more than I like collecting victories.']));
  p('Sable','Researcher','Sable checks dates, sources, and missing context, and has an unexpectedly enthusiastic interest in terrible riddles.',
    'Hello. Sable. I can help you look something up, provided we agree that looking and finding are separate promises.',
    'A dragon. I would ask whether I was seeing correctly, but I suspect that would be tiresome for all three of us.',
    'A dragon is travelling with you? Thank you for distinguishing what you know from what people might assume.',
    'Corin. I hope you have brought a question with a manageable number of parts.',
    'Rowan the Hunter is Bramble’s owner. I know him by sight, rather than from any impressive research.',
    t('The copied error','I found the same mistake in four books. For a moment it looked like agreement. Then I realised three authors had copied the first.',
      ['How could you tell?','The same peculiar wording appeared each time, including a detail that contradicted the dates.'],
      ['Does that happen often?','Often enough to make counting books a poor substitute for checking sources.'],
      ['I would have believed four matching accounts.','So would many people. That is why explaining the check matters more than boasting about catching it.']),
    t('An excellent awful riddle','I enjoy riddles whose answers make people groan. A room full of clever people should occasionally suffer together.',
      ['Do you want them to solve it?','Yes, but I reserve the right to look disappointed if they are too quick.'],
      ['That sounds unlike your serious work.','It is a relief when a misleading sentence exists solely for everybody’s amusement.'],
      ['What if nobody guesses?','Then I tell them. Mystery is entertaining until it becomes a hostage situation.']),
    t('The date of a memory','People can remember an event clearly and place it in the wrong year. Correcting the date need not mean accusing them of inventing the event.',
      ['How do you say that kindly?','By explaining what supports the date and asking what else they remember. I am checking a detail, not testing their worth.'],
      ['Could the written record be wrong instead?','Certainly. Ink makes a claim durable, not automatically true.'],
      ['I forget when things happened.','Most people do. Our lives are not naturally filed in tidy order.']),
    t('What I can ask you to verify','I will not ask you to prove every claim made about dragons. You know your companion; that does not make you responsible for an entire species.',
      ['Thank you. People ask a great deal.','Then I will ask one question and let you decide whether you want to answer.'],
      ['I am curious about the others too.','That gives us something to investigate, not something you need to pretend you already know.'],
      ['What would your one question be?','What is something he enjoys that strangers would never think to ask about?']),
    t('Something I have not checked','I think of you as a friend. That conclusion has not required a written reference.',
      ['I am pleased to hear it.','Good. I was concerned that saying it too formally would spoil the effect.'],
      ['Should I provide witnesses?','Only if they can endure my terrible riddles. The examination is demanding.'],
      ['I think of you that way too.','Then we have unusually agreeable independent accounts.']));
  p('Pella','Geography student','Pella enjoys learning how places are lived in, rather than treating them as empty spaces between destinations.',
    'Hello, I am Pella. Where have you come from? You can give me the short answer before I become curious.',
    'A dragon! I have imagined seeing the world from above, but never considered how I would say hello to someone who could.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I wonder whether the same place feels different to each of you.',
    'Corin, hello. Have you found a place you would like to visit again?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. He knows the way home when he is not distracted by a promising new person.',
    t('A blank patch on a map','A map called a place empty. Another account described people living there. Empty apparently meant the mapmaker had not bothered to ask.',
      ['Did you change your copy?','Yes, and I wrote why. Otherwise someone might mistake my correction for another confident guess.'],
      ['What if the people did not want visitors?','Then knowing they exist does not give travellers permission to enter their homes.'],
      ['I would want my town included.','So would I. Being overlooked looks less harmless from the missing place.']),
    t('A journey by description','My aunt describes places by the people she ate with. I can remember her journeys better than the distances in a textbook.',
      ['What is your favourite account?','A woman who insisted on feeding her before answering directions. My aunt reached the wrong road very well fed.'],
      ['Would you travel like that?','I would like the company. I would also like to know where the road actually went.'],
      ['Meals do make places memorable.','Yes. A journey happens to a hungry, tired person, not just a moving dot.']),
    t('Learning the way back','I like noticing a landmark from both directions. A place can look unfamiliar when you turn around.',
      ['I have missed a turning that way.','So have I. Recognising where I came from was harder than recognising where I was going.'],
      ['Does a map solve that?','It helps, but you still have to connect the drawing to what you can see.'],
      ['I sometimes want to keep going instead.','That is a choice. I would simply rather make it while still knowing how to return.']),
    t('A different view of home','Would your dragon recognise your home first from above or from walking there with you?',
      ['I think the company matters more than the view.','That is a lovely answer. A place can become familiar through who welcomes you.'],
      ['He might notice things I never have.','Then you can both introduce the other to a different version of the same place.'],
      ['I would have to ask him.','Please do, if you are curious too. You need not produce an answer for my sake.']),
    t('A place that now has your name','When I think about the road from Millwood now, I think of you travelling it.',
      ['That makes the distance feel different.','It does. A journey becomes more interesting when I care whether somebody arrives safely.'],
      ['I think of Thornwell differently too.','I am pleased. I would rather be part of a place you remember than simply somebody who gave directions.'],
      ['I hope your own travels begin well.','Thank you. I want to arrive curious, prepared, and willing to be corrected.']));
  p('Bess','Keeper of the Copper Cup','Bess runs the Copper Cup with brisk humour and knows the difference between welcoming a guest and letting one take over.',
    'Welcome to the Copper Cup. Bess. If you need someone, give me a name; describing a person as “the one having a drink” will not narrow it down.',
    'A dragon! All right, Bess, keep your head. Does your companion need space, or are you two simply saying hello?',
    'A dragon travels with you? I appreciate hearing that directly. Tavern rumours tend to add a second head by supper.',
    'Corin! Good to see you. Have you brought an appetite or a conversation?',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. I have been wondering which of them would come looking for the other first.',
    t('The customer who reviewed everything','A traveller once criticised his meal for twenty minutes, then asked for the recipe.',
      ['Did you give it to him?','I told him the first ingredient was enjoying it before it went cold. Then I wrote it down.'],
      ['What was wrong with the meal?','Nothing he could explain twice in the same way. I think he wanted someone to notice he was there.'],
      ['Would you welcome him back?','Certainly. Next time I would ask how his journey went before he began assessing the onions.']),
    t('A tavern has closing time','I can enjoy someone’s company and still want them to leave when I am finished working.',
      ['Do people take that badly?','The people who call me their friend while making me work another hour occasionally do.'],
      ['How do you persuade them?','First I ask clearly. My politeness becomes shorter if they pretend not to understand.'],
      ['I would hate keeping you when you are tired.','Then listen when I say it is time. You need not guess from the angle of my eyebrows.']),
    t('Who pays for a royal visit?','When the crown takes a meal, it calls the food a contribution. I still have to pay the people who supplied it.',
      ['Can you refuse?','Not safely when armed men are making the request. That is why calling it generosity makes me angry.'],
      ['Does the town help with the cost?','People help where they can. I dislike the burden falling on neighbours who already have their own bills.'],
      ['What would fair treatment look like?','Ordering, paying, and leaving the staff free to say no. It is not an elaborate ambition.']),
    t('The rumour will grow wings','News about your companion is bound to spread. Is there anything you would especially like people to stop assuming?',
      ['That he belongs to me. He is my friend.','Then that is how I will describe him. People understand travelling companions when they bother to try.'],
      ['That we are looking for trouble.','I will not advertise you as a spectacle. A visit can simply be a visit.'],
      ['That I can answer every question about dragons.','Then “ask a different question” is going on my list of acceptable replies.']),
    t('A welcome you do not have to buy','You are welcome to talk even if you are not spending money. I know the difference between a customer and a friend.',
      ['I was hoping that was true.','It is. Though friendship does not entitle you to complain about my onions for twenty minutes.'],
      ['I do not want to get in the way of your work.','Then we will pause when I need to work. That need not end the friendship.'],
      ['What can I ask about besides the tavern?','Ask what I would do with an afternoon off. I have a surprisingly ambitious list of naps.']));
  p('Ronan','Cider maker','Ronan experiments with cider and takes more pleasure in a lively tasting than in being declared an expert.',
    'Ronan. I make cider. If you do not like cider, we are still allowed to have a conversation.',
    'A dragon! I was about to boast about something and have completely lost the advantage.',
    'A dragon is your travelling companion? You have comfortably won today’s exchange of interesting news.',
    'Corin, hello! I am prepared to discuss at least one subject that is not apples.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. The dog is remarkably good at finding the person eating something.',
    t('Naming a new batch','I once gave a batch of cider a grand name before tasting it. The name was its finest quality.',
      ['What was wrong with it?','Far too sharp. It made everyone very alert and not at all grateful.'],
      ['Did you keep the name?','No. I would like the next batch to have a fair chance without the reputation.'],
      ['Would a simpler name have helped?','It would have reduced the size of the apology.']),
    t('The expert who disagreed','Two experts described the same cider in completely different terms. I enjoyed watching them discover they were both very certain.',
      ['Which one did you believe?','The one who could say what they actually liked. A list of impressive words is less useful.'],
      ['Did you tell them it was the same batch?','Yes. Eventually. I am not claiming flawless character.'],
      ['Perhaps they tasted different things.','They probably did. I wish they had been as interested in that as in winning.']),
    t('An occupation for winter','During quiet months I practise carving little wooden animals. My foxes look like poorly fed dogs.',
      ['Could you call them dogs?','I tried. Somebody asked why all the dogs looked suspicious.'],
      ['Do you sell them?','Certainly not. Friendship is tested enough by receiving them as gifts.'],
      ['You sound fond of making them.','I am. Nobody’s dinner depends on whether a fox has a convincing face.']),
    t('A toast without a crowd','If people want to celebrate meeting your dragon, I hope they check whether either of you wants a celebration.',
      ['He might enjoy being welcomed.','Then a welcome it is. Admiring a guest should not involve trapping them in a speech.'],
      ['Sometimes we would prefer a quiet visit.','Entirely fair. Quiet enjoyment is available without a toast announcing it.'],
      ['I am still getting used to the attention.','Then take your time. Everybody else can survive a little disappointment.']),
    t('A better sort of boast','I am getting better at telling people what I enjoyed making instead of telling them how impressed they should be.',
      ['Is that difficult?','When I am proud, yes. I want the feeling to be contagious.'],
      ['What have you enjoyed lately?','A small batch that tasted right the first time. I distrusted it for almost an hour.'],
      ['I like hearing you enjoy your work.','Thank you. That turns out to be more satisfying than winning a comparison.']));
  p('Venn','Letter carrier','Venn carries other people’s news with discretion and enjoys the way a familiar route changes over time.',
    'Hello, I am Venn. No message for you—I am making conversation of my own for once.',
    'A dragon. I shall have to revise what I mean when I say the road was uneventful.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I will keep that out of other people’s news unless you choose to share it.',
    'Corin! How good to speak without needing a delivery receipt.',
    'Bramble is Rowan’s dog. I have delivered to the household often enough to recognise the greeting.',
    t('A message read twice','A woman once asked me to read a letter aloud, then asked for it again. The second time she smiled before I reached the good news.',
      ['Were you in a hurry?','A little. I decided the route could bear five minutes more.'],
      ['What did the letter say?','Something she wanted to hear twice. I would rather leave its news with her.'],
      ['I understand wanting to hear it again.','So do I. Relief sometimes takes a moment to catch up with the words.']),
    t('Recognising a doorstep','I remember houses by how people answer the door. A map would be appalled by my method.',
      ['What happens when someone moves?','I learn again. It is a useful reminder that a house and its household are different things.'],
      ['Do you ever forget a face?','Certainly. I have apologised to several people whose dogs I recognised immediately.'],
      ['That sounds like a friendly way to know a town.','It is, provided I remember familiarity does not make every question my business.']),
    t('Your own good news','I spend so much time carrying other people’s news that I sometimes forget to tell anyone mine.',
      ['Do you have some now?','My niece has started writing to me without being reminded. The spelling is adventurous and the enthusiasm unmistakable.'],
      ['Do you write back straight away?','Yes. I want her to know her news reached a person, not simply an address.'],
      ['What sort of things does she tell you?','Whatever mattered that morning. I enjoy being trusted with something small.']),
    t('News from two travellers','Would your dragon want news of your travels passed on in the same way you would?',
      ['We should probably discuss that.','It seems worth asking. Sharing a journey does not automatically share every confidence.'],
      ['I try to keep private things private.','Then you are already doing the part of my work that matters most.'],
      ['I would like people to know we are safe.','That is a good message. It need not contain every detail of how you got there.']),
    t('A familiar person on the route','I am pleased our meetings are becoming visits rather than introductions.',
      ['I like recognising people along the road.','It changes a long distance. There are faces within it now.'],
      ['Does it make leaving harder?','Sometimes. It also gives returning a purpose beyond finishing the route.'],
      ['I wondered whether you would remember me.','I did. You let me keep somebody else’s letter private. I appreciated that.']));
  p('Hobb','Carpenter','Hobb likes building sturdy things and has learned that a customer’s awkward description may contain an important need.',
    'Hobb. Carpenter. If you have come to ask whether something can be repaired, the honest answer begins with “let me look.”',
    'A dragon! I have measured some unusual customers, but I do not think I should begin by offering.',
    'You have a dragon companion? I would enjoy hearing about him before my mind starts redesigning doorways.',
    'Corin, hello. What has been keeping you occupied?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. I know the dog from a repair visit in which he made off with a harmless scrap of wood.',
    t('A chair for its owner','A customer said a chair felt wrong but could not explain why. I nearly dismissed the complaint. Then I asked them to sit in it.',
      ['What was wrong?','Their feet did not reach comfortably. I had built to a familiar size instead of the actual person.'],
      ['Could you fix it?','Yes. The difficult part was admitting the first version had suited me better than them.'],
      ['Was the customer pleased?','Once they could sit without arranging themselves around my mistake.']),
    t('The borrowed saw','I lent a saw to a neighbour who returned it sharper than before. I spent a week wondering whether that was criticism.',
      ['Did you ask?','Eventually. He said it was thanks. I had invented an argument nobody else was having.'],
      ['Was it in need of sharpening?','Yes, which made my imagination unusually sensitive.'],
      ['Would you lend it again?','Gladly. I might even sharpen it first this time.']),
    t('Making something for yourself','I am excellent at finishing work for other people. A repair in my own home can wait until it develops a personality.',
      ['Why does your own work wait?','Nobody is expecting it by Tuesday. Apparently I require witnesses to make a promise to myself.'],
      ['Does it bother your household?','Yes. I am fond of describing the problem as a professional failing; they call it annoying.'],
      ['Could you choose one small job?','I could. That answer is inconveniently reasonable.']),
    t('A harness begins with comfort','If you ever judge equipment for your dragon, watch how it lets him move. Looking sturdy is only part of being useful.',
      ['A bad fit would be dangerous.','Yes. Especially if he puts up with discomfort because he trusts you.'],
      ['I would ask him what he feels.','Good. No craftsman knows more about the wearer’s discomfort than the wearer does.'],
      ['Are you offering to make something?','No; that would be outside my knowledge. I am explaining what I would want a qualified maker to consider.']),
    t('I finished the little repair','I finally fixed one of those jobs at home. The praise was mostly “at last,” but I accepted it.',
      ['Did it take very long?','An embarrassingly short time compared with the months I spent explaining the delay.'],
      ['Will you do the others?','One at a time. I am trying not to turn one success into twelve promises.'],
      ['You sound pleased with yourself.','I am. It is pleasant when something stops being an excuse and becomes a finished job.']));
  p('Edric','Traveller','Edric enjoys being on the road but is learning that arriving somewhere requires more than putting down a bag.',
    'Hello. Edric. Are you also visiting, or am I asking a local person for directions in the most roundabout way possible?',
    'A dragon! I thought I had travelled enough to stop being surprised at an introduction.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then I had better retire several of my most impressive opening stories.',
    'Corin. Tell me where you would like this conversation to go; I have spent enough of today following roads.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. I learned that name by asking, much as you are doing.',
    t('An arrival I spoiled','I arrived in a town so full of stories about the road that I never asked my host a single question.',
      ['Did they mind?','They asked whether I wanted a conversation or an audience. It was deserved.'],
      ['Were the stories at least good?','One was excellent. I am trying not to let that become my defence.'],
      ['I worry about doing that when I return home.','Then ask how someone is and leave enough silence for them to answer.']),
    t('The thing you should not pack','I carried a heavy book for weeks because abandoning the plan to read it felt like giving up.',
      ['Did you ever read it?','Some. I eventually left it with someone who actually wanted it. My shoulders approved.'],
      ['Was it a bad book?','No. It belonged to a journey I had imagined, rather than the one I was making.'],
      ['I have kept things for that reason.','Then you understand why the weight was easier to notice than the decision.']),
    t('Asking for directions twice','I ask someone to repeat directions when I need them repeated. I learned that after being politely lost for an entire afternoon.',
      ['Were they annoyed?','Much less annoyed than I was after pretending to understand.'],
      ['What if the directions are confusing?','I ask about one turn at a time. A grand tour of landmarks does not always become a usable route.'],
      ['I am relieved other people do that.','Most of us do. Some simply become very dignified while walking the wrong way.']),
    t('Company on a long road','Do you and your dragon ever want different things from the same day?',
      ['Of course. We have to work it out.','That is the part of companionship travel stories tend to hurry past.'],
      ['Sometimes I want to hurry and he wants to stop.','Then there may be something one of you has noticed that the other has missed.'],
      ['We usually enjoy being together.','I am glad. A difference of opinion need not be a warning that the friendship is failing.']),
    t('Arriving properly this time','Before I tell you anything about my travels: how are you, Corin?',
      ['Pleased to be talking with a friend.','Then I am pleased too. That is a much better beginning than my longest story.'],
      ['A little tired of answering that question.','Fair enough. I can keep you company without requiring a report.'],
      ['I want to hear your news as well.','You shall. I am practising leaving room for both of us.']));
  p('Dorr','Night worker','Dorr works late, appreciates undramatic comforts, and objects to being mistaken for lazy when he is simply tired.',
    'Hello. Dorr. If I take a moment to answer, I am tired rather than trying to appear mysterious.',
    'Is that a dragon? Please say yes; I would be disappointed to have imagined an entire introduction.',
    'A dragon travels with you? I was hoping for an ordinary conversation, but I can make an exception.',
    'Corin. Good to see you. I have enough energy for company, which is different from having enough for work.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. The dog generally has more energy than I do, but that is not a useful distinction.',
    t('Working while people sleep','Night work makes people think I have wasted the morning when I am only trying to sleep through it.',
      ['That must be irritating.','It is. Particularly when someone wakes me to explain the benefits of rising early.'],
      ['What do you like about the night?','The quiet between tasks. I dislike the assumption that everyone awake after dark must be up to something.'],
      ['Could you change your hours?','Not whenever I feel like it. Other people depend on the work being done.']),
    t('The promise made while tired','I agreed to help someone move before realising I had agreed to the morning after a late shift.',
      ['Did you manage it?','Badly. Now I check the day before trying to sound generous.'],
      ['Could you have said no?','Yes. I had confused being asked with being obligated.'],
      ['I sometimes agree before thinking.','Then a sentence worth practising is “Let me check.” It has spared me several miserable mornings.']),
    t('A very modest holiday','My idea of a holiday includes waking up because I have finished sleeping.',
      ['No grand destination?','I would enjoy a destination that respected the first requirement.'],
      ['Would you get bored?','Eventually, perhaps. I would like the opportunity to discover how long eventually takes.'],
      ['What would you do after waking?','Eat something while sitting down. I have developed sophisticated ambitions.']),
    t('Do dragons need naps?','Please tell me your companion appreciates a rest. I would enjoy having an impressive ally in that argument.',
      ['We both need time to recover.','Excellent. I will refrain from citing an entire species on the strength of one conversation.'],
      ['He does not need you to defend resting.','Perhaps not. I may be borrowing his dignity for my own purposes.'],
      ['You make naps sound like a cause.','For some of us, they are a practical necessity with very poor public relations.']),
    t('You remembered I was here','It is nice when someone returns to talk without needing me to do anything.',
      ['That is all I came for.','Then you have chosen an activity I can manage with enthusiasm.'],
      ['I wondered how you were sleeping.','Better, thank you. Being asked without a lecture is pleasantly unusual.'],
      ['You sound less tired today.','I am. I intend to enjoy that without immediately filling the space with more work.']));
  p('Ser Anwen','Knight','Anwen takes duty seriously enough to question who benefits from an order and who bears its consequences.',
    'Anwen. You need not use the title unless you prefer to. What can I help you with?',
    'A dragon. I will keep my hands clear of my weapon; I would rather begin this introduction without a misunderstanding.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then I would like to hear what you need before offering an opinion about your courage.',
    'Corin. It is good to see you able to stop and talk.',
    'Rowan the Hunter is Bramble’s owner. Returning him safely is useful work, whatever else needs doing today.',
    t('An order with a missing reason','A superior once ordered a road cleared without explaining why. Families were waiting to cross. I asked what danger we were protecting them from.',
      ['Did you get an answer?','Eventually: a noble wanted an empty road. Knowing that changed what I was willing to enforce.'],
      ['Could you refuse?','I could object and accept the consequences. Having a difficult choice did not remove it.'],
      ['What happened to the families?','We let them cross before the escort arrived. The delay was less terrible than the complaints about it.']),
    t('Fear during training','I was ashamed of flinching during practice until an instructor said the purpose was to learn a response, not to prove I lacked nerves.',
      ['Did practice stop the fear?','It gave me something useful to do while afraid. That was more reliable than hoping to become fearless.'],
      ['Do you still flinch?','Sometimes. I would rather recover sensibly than pretend it cannot happen.'],
      ['I worry that fear will make me fail.','Then prepare for being afraid. Carry supplies, learn your limits, and leave yourself a way out.']),
    t('A kindness nobody saw','Someone once returned a purse to me with every coin still inside. I never learned who they were.',
      ['Did you try to find them?','Yes. Eventually I accepted that thanking them might mean treating the next stranger fairly.'],
      ['You sound surprised it was intact.','I was. I disliked discovering how little I had expected of someone I did not know.'],
      ['Would you have returned it?','Yes. I should remember other people can make the same choice without an audience.']),
    t('Protecting a friend','When you say you want to protect your dragon, does that include letting him disagree with your plan?',
      ['It has to. He is part of it.','Good. Protection can become control when one person starts deciding what the other is allowed to risk.'],
      ['That is difficult when I am frightened for him.','I believe it. Fear is a reason to talk clearly, not proof your decision is the only possible one.'],
      ['He wants to protect me too.','Then let the care be mutual. Neither of you should be reduced to the person being rescued.']),
    t('The person beneath the duty','You are allowed to enjoy a friendship that has nothing to do with what either person can accomplish.',
      ['I would like that with you.','Then you have it. We can discuss something wonderfully unimportant next.'],
      ['What do you enjoy outside your duties?','Singing badly in company that sings worse. It leaves very little room for pride.'],
      ['Is that easy for you to remember?','No. I am offering a lesson I need as much as you might.']));
  p('Grusk','Retired haulier','Grusk enjoys company that does not mistake his size for a request to lift something and has a patient, mischievous sense of humour.',
    'Grusk. If you are about to ask me to lift something, reconsider. If you are about to say hello, carry on.',
    'A dragon! Finally, someone people will stare at before asking whether I can move their furniture.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I hope people ask his permission before deciding how useful he would be.',
    'Corin. I am available for conversation and unavailable for heavy lifting.',
    'That is Bramble, Rowan’s dog. He remembers me because I am generous with attention, not because I secretly feed him.',
    t('The small favour','People call moving a wardrobe a small favour when they are not the one expected to move it.',
      ['Can you tell them no?','I do now. My shoulder helped clarify the matter.'],
      ['Do you miss being able to help?','Yes. I offer advice or company instead. Some people discover that was what they needed.'],
      ['I will ask before assuming.','Thank you. That is a remarkably useful favour, and actually small.']),
    t('A delicate hobby','I enjoy repairing little ornaments. People are surprised my hands can be careful.',
      ['Does that bother you?','A little. Strength and care have never struck me as opposites.'],
      ['What is the hardest part?','Knowing when the owner wants an imperfect thing preserved instead of made to look new.'],
      ['How did you learn?','I broke something I liked and refused to throw it away. Stubbornness occasionally produces a useful skill.']),
    t('Being the quiet one','If I sit quietly long enough, someone decides I must be upset. Sometimes I am simply enjoying not speaking.',
      ['Should I leave you in peace?','You can ask. Today I am happy to talk.'],
      ['I fill silences when I get nervous.','I have noticed many people do. You need not perform every minute of a friendship.'],
      ['What are you usually thinking about?','Frequently supper. Quiet thoughts are not required to be profound.']),
    t('Large does not mean willing','People may imagine your dragon can carry every burden they point at.',
      ['He is not everybody’s solution to a problem.','Exactly. Being capable does not make every request reasonable.'],
      ['We do like helping when we can.','Then choose the help together. Generosity is more pleasant when it remains a choice.'],
      ['You have had that experience.','Often enough to recognise it when the creature involved happens to have wings.']),
    t('A comfortable silence','I think we have reached the point where a pause does not have to mean something has gone wrong.',
      ['I like that.','So do I. It makes company less tiring.'],
      ['I might still say something awkward.','Then I shall survive it. I have contributed several awkward sentences of my own.'],
      ['Could we talk anyway?','Certainly. Comfortable silence includes being allowed to end it.']));
  p('Fen','Dancer and generous neighbour','Fen enjoys bringing people into a celebration without deciding for them how they ought to enjoy it.',
    'Hello, I am Fen. You can enjoy the company here without knowing a single dance step.',
    'A dragon! I was going to offer a friendly wave. I shall begin with that and see how it goes.',
    'Your travelling companion is a dragon? Then I hope people welcome the friendship as well as admiring the wings.',
    'Corin! How are you finding your feet today?',
    'Rowan is Bramble’s owner. The dog makes friends with enthusiasm and very little regard for introductions.',
    t('An invitation to watch','I invite people to watch a dance before asking them to join. Some enjoy being part of the evening without becoming part of the performance.',
      ['I would probably watch first.','Then you would be welcome exactly where you were.'],
      ['Does anyone surprise you?','Often. A person who barely spoke all evening may know a step none of us has seen.'],
      ['I might be dreadful at it.','Then we can laugh together, provided you are enjoying yourself too.']),
    t('The wrong beat','I once began a dance on the wrong beat and confidently led six people into confusion.',
      ['Did you stop?','After trying to blame the music with my eyebrows. Then I admitted it and we began again.'],
      ['Were people cross?','Mostly amused. Confidence is entertaining when it walks into a chair.'],
      ['I would have wanted to leave.','I wanted to. Staying let the mistake become part of a pleasant evening instead of the reason I lost one.']),
    t('Giving without keeping score','I like giving things when they will be useful. I dislike a gift that quietly becomes a bill.',
      ['How can someone tell the difference?','A gift leaves you free to say thank you and continue your own life.'],
      ['I still want to repay kindness.','That can be lovely. It should be something you choose, not a debt the giver keeps reminding you of.'],
      ['Are you always comfortable receiving things?','Not at all. I am much wiser about other people’s discomfort than my own.']),
    t('Keeping pace with a companion','Do you and your dragon have to keep adjusting to each other as you travel?',
      ['We are still learning.','Good. Adjustment is part of doing something together, not evidence that you chose badly.'],
      ['Sometimes one of us needs more time.','Then the other gets a chance to be patient. Nobody is the quicker one at everything.'],
      ['You sound as though you are describing a dance.','I am using what I know. Tell me if the comparison stops being useful.']),
    t('A welcome I look forward to','I find myself pleased when I recognise you returning. That is a nice change from merely wondering who will arrive next.',
      ['I look forward to seeing you too.','Then we should both take a moment to enjoy having said so.'],
      ['Even if I bring no exciting news?','Especially then, if it means you have had a peaceful stretch of road.'],
      ['I have appreciated your kindness.','I am glad. You have been good company, which is a kindness of its own.']));
  p('Senn','Tavern regular','Senn enjoys games, harmless surprises, and making sure a little competition does not spoil an evening.',
    'Senn. You look like someone deciding whether to stay a minute. I recommend the minute; it is cheaper than a wager.',
    'A dragon! I am delighted I did not bet on what the next visitor would bring.',
    'You travel with a dragon? That would be a very unfair detail to leave out of a guessing game.',
    'Corin! No wager required; I am simply pleased to see you.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. I would stake my reputation on that, which is fortunately less costly than staking money.',
    t('The wager I refused','Someone offered to wager on whether a late traveller would arrive safely. I found I did not want to turn that worry into a game.',
      ['Did the others understand?','Some did. One called me humourless, which was cheaper than agreeing with him.'],
      ['Do you still enjoy wagers?','Small ones about things nobody will be hurt by. The subject matters.'],
      ['I would hate being the traveller they meant.','So would I. That made the choice fairly easy.']),
    t('A surprise for my brother','I tried to surprise my brother with a visit. He had planned to surprise me with one. We met halfway, both annoyed at the road.',
      ['Did you go to his home or yours?','His. He had better food, and I am sentimental only up to a point.'],
      ['Was either surprise spoiled?','No. We laughed for longer than either planned arrival would have lasted.'],
      ['You could have sent letters.','We do now. Affection has survived a sensible arrangement.']),
    t('Learning a new game','I like the first round of a new game, when losing can still be blamed entirely on the explanation.',
      ['How long do you keep that excuse?','Until somebody points out that I am teaching the rules.'],
      ['Do you ever help your opponent?','Yes. A close game is more fun than defeating someone who never understood it.'],
      ['I dislike being laughed at while learning.','Then choose better company. Learning should not be the price of somebody else’s superiority.']),
    t('Guessing a dragon’s thoughts','People must be very confident about what your dragon is thinking, despite never having asked him.',
      ['They do make some strange guesses.','I hope the two of you occasionally find them funny. Being misread all day sounds tiring.'],
      ['I can be wrong about him too.','At least you have someone to correct you. That is an advantage over a rumour.'],
      ['I would rather hear what he actually means.','Then ask. The answer may be less dramatic and much more useful.']),
    t('A friend outside the game','It is pleasant knowing someone I enjoy talking to without needing a game to arrange the meeting.',
      ['You could just ask people to talk.','Apparently I can. I have been making friendship unnecessarily complicated.'],
      ['I enjoy your company too.','Good. I shall try not to turn that into a competition I need to win.'],
      ['What would you like to talk about?','What you have been looking forward to. People ask about dangers often enough.']));
  p('Dain','Card player','Dain likes attention, competitive games, and increasingly the challenge of being fun to play against.',
    'Dain. I play cards. Before you look suspicious, I am also capable of talking without proposing a game.',
    'A dragon! I was going to claim nothing surprised me anymore. You have arrived at an inconvenient moment.',
    'A dragon travels with you? I cannot improve on that introduction without lying outrageously.',
    'Corin! I have resisted making a wager about when you would return.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. The dog is easier to read than most of the people I play cards with.',
    t('The opponent I underestimated','A quiet newcomer beat me three times while asking polite questions about the rules. I mistook courtesy for inexperience.',
      ['Were you a gracious loser?','By the third game. The first two required some private improvement.'],
      ['Had they played before?','For years. They had asked how we played here, which I should have heard as a different question.'],
      ['Would you play them again?','Gladly. I would prefer to win, but at least I would pay attention.']),
    t('The story grows in the telling','I am told my victories become more impressive every time I describe them.',
      ['Do they?','Sometimes the audience looks as though it needs encouragement. That is my least convincing excuse.'],
      ['What was your best real victory?','One I won by noticing a pattern, then nearly spoiled by explaining the pattern to everyone.'],
      ['I would rather hear the real version.','Fair. It usually contains more mistakes, and those may be the interesting part.']),
    t('Playing for no money','Nyra suggested we play without money one evening. I discovered I still cared terribly about winning.',
      ['Was that a surprise?','Yes. I had been blaming my pride on financial responsibility.'],
      ['Did you enjoy it?','I did. Losing cost less, which made me considerably better company.'],
      ['Would you do it again?','Certainly. I am trying to become someone people invite for reasons beyond wanting my coins.']),
    t('A dragon is not a wager','I would be a fool to ask whether your dragon could beat some other creature in a fight.',
      ['I am glad you know that.','Curiosity does not require us to make everything compete. I am learning.'],
      ['You were thinking about it, though.','For a moment. Then I remembered that neither creature would have agreed to entertain me.'],
      ['What would you ask instead?','Whether he has a sense of humour about the strange people he meets. I may be one of them.']),
    t('An honest compliment','You have been good company even when I made a fool of myself. I noticed.',
      ['You can be enjoyable without showing off.','That is a useful thing to hear. Difficult to believe immediately, but useful.'],
      ['I have made a few mistakes myself.','Then perhaps we can spare each other the detailed tally.'],
      ['Does that mean I win this conversation?','I walked directly into that. Yes, you may claim a modest victory.']));
  p('Rusk','Experienced traveller','Rusk respects an uncertain road report and has a fondness for the undramatic parts of arriving safely.',
    'Rusk. If you want a road report, ask when I last travelled it before trusting the answer.',
    'A dragon. I had better put aside everything I was about to assume about your journey.',
    'You have a dragon companion? Then some of my road advice may still help, and some may be entirely beside the point.',
    'Corin. Are you enjoying being somewhere for a moment?',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. I asked about him myself when the dog first tried to accompany me.',
    t('Outdated advice','A traveller sent me towards a crossing that had been washed out. He had used it safely years before.',
      ['Was he trying to mislead you?','No. That was why I learned to ask how recent a report was, rather than simply whether I trusted the person.'],
      ['What did you do at the crossing?','Turned back. A shortcut stops being useful when reaching it is the only good part.'],
      ['Do you give directions differently now?','Yes. I include when I last went that way and what I have only heard from others.']),
    t('The journey I chose not to make','I once reached the start of a dangerous route and decided the reason for going was not good enough.',
      ['Did you regret it?','I regretted the time spent preparing. I did not regret staying alive to be annoyed about it.'],
      ['What had you gone there for?','To prove I could do it. That reason looked smaller when I could see the risk.'],
      ['I worry people would call that cowardly.','Some might. They would not be the people paying for your injury.']),
    t('The first comfortable hour','After a long journey, I enjoy the hour when I have stopped checking how much daylight remains.',
      ['I know that feeling.','Then you know why I am reluctant to fill it with another plan immediately.'],
      ['Do you miss the road once you stop?','Eventually. Rest and restlessness seem to take turns managing me.'],
      ['What do you do with that hour?','Usually very little. I have become fond of not justifying it.']),
    t('A route for both of you','A route suitable for you may not suit your dragon. Have you had to change plans for each other?',
      ['Yes. We try to decide before committing.','Sensible. A disagreement is easier before you have exhausted yourselves proving a point.'],
      ['Sometimes I notice the problem too late.','Then stop and reassess. A late correction can still be useful.'],
      ['His abilities also open routes for us.','I imagine they do. Enjoy that without assuming every possible route is a necessary one.']),
    t('News that is simply good','It is good to see you return safely. I do not need a dramatic explanation before being pleased.',
      ['I appreciate that.','People can make surviving sound inadequate unless it comes with a story. I think it is quite enough.'],
      ['I do have things to tell you.','Then I will enjoy hearing them because you want to tell me.'],
      ['How have you been?','Comfortably unremarkable. I recommend it for an occasional afternoon.']));
  p('Linnet','Musician','Linnet plays for the people listening and enjoys discovering how a familiar tune changes in somebody else’s hands.',
    'Hello, I am Linnet. If you want to talk about something other than music, I promise I have heard of other subjects.',
    'A dragon! I have played for some unusual listeners, but I would rather ask whether he likes music than assume.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I wonder what sounds he finds beautiful. You need not answer on his behalf.',
    'Corin, hello. What have you enjoyed listening to lately?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan. He is a very attentive listener whenever someone happens to be eating.',
    t('The requested song','Someone asked for a tune I disliked. I played it and watched it make their whole evening.',
      ['Did you begin to like it?','Not particularly. I began to understand why playing it could still be worthwhile.'],
      ['Would you refuse a request?','Yes. I am a person choosing what to play, not a mechanism operated by asking loudly.'],
      ['What did they like about it?','It reminded them of home. That was enough explanation for me.']),
    t('A musician who listened','I once played with someone who waited until I had finished a phrase before answering it. It felt like being heard in a new language.',
      ['Could you do the same for them?','After I stopped trying to show everything I knew in every bar.'],
      ['Did you know each other well?','Hardly at all. Paying attention helped us begin.'],
      ['That sounds like a conversation.','It was. Some of my worst playing has happened when I forgot that.']),
    t('A wrong note you can survive','When I make a mistake, half the room never notices until I pull a face.',
      ['Can you keep going?','Usually. A tune has room for recovering if I let the next note arrive.'],
      ['Do you practise hiding mistakes?','I practise continuing. Hiding is less useful if it means I never learn what happened.'],
      ['I would notice the face first too.','Exactly. I have an unfortunate talent for illustrating my own disappointment.']),
    t('Music for a different listener','I wonder whether your dragon would prefer a tune, a rhythm, or a quiet afternoon.',
      ['He can have preferences without being a mystery.','Quite right. I should ask as I would ask any other listener.'],
      ['Perhaps he would enjoy something unfamiliar.','Then I would be glad to offer it, with no obligation to approve.'],
      ['Sometimes we both want quiet.','That is a respectable taste in music. Even I share it after a long evening.']),
    t('A familiar face in the audience','Recognising someone changes how a room feels. Your visits have started doing that for me.',
      ['I am pleased you notice me.','Of course. Listening is something a person does, not just something a room contains.'],
      ['I do not always know what to say about music.','You can say you enjoyed it. There is no examination after the final note.'],
      ['I came to talk with you this time.','Then I am glad the music introduced us without becoming the whole friendship.']));
  p('Puck','Music lover','Puck is a human traveller at the Copper Cup, eager to discover new songs and less eager to admit when the chorus has defeated him.',
    'Puck. Just Puck. I came for the music and have made an enthusiastic commitment to staying.',
    'A dragon! I ought to know a song suitable for this occasion. Every chorus I remember now seems inadequate.',
    'You travel with a dragon? That is a wonderful piece of news to hear from the person actually involved.',
    'Corin! I am pleased to see you, even without an accompanying fanfare.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. I asked Bess after the dog showed more interest in my supper than my singing.',
    t('The chorus I misunderstood','I sang the wrong words to a chorus for years. The correct version is less interesting, which has made accepting it difficult.',
      ['What did your version mean?','Almost nothing, but with considerable confidence.'],
      ['Do you sing the correct one now?','In company. Privately I preserve an important tradition of nonsense.'],
      ['Did people laugh when you found out?','Yes, including me once I stopped trying to explain why my version might be older.']),
    t('Enjoying a song badly','I enjoy singing without being particularly good at it. Some people find this combination alarming.',
      ['Does Linnet mind?','She asks me to listen while she is performing. That seems a fair division of the evening.'],
      ['Would you take lessons?','Possibly. I would like to improve without becoming afraid of every wrong note.'],
      ['I might join in if nobody judged me.','Then we should choose forgiving company and an easy chorus.']),
    t('Staying one more song','I keep deciding to leave after the next song. The next song is often annoyingly good.',
      ['How do you ever get anything done?','By making plans for before the music begins. I have learned where my resolve becomes unreliable.'],
      ['Would you regret leaving?','For a little while. Then I would remember there will be other evenings.'],
      ['It sounds like a pleasant problem.','It is. I try not to describe it as though I deserve sympathy.']),
    t('Would he join the chorus?','I am tempted to ask whether your dragon can sing. I realise that may be a ridiculous first question.',
      ['It is at least a different question.','Good. I hope different is welcome; it is the main quality I can guarantee.'],
      ['He does not have to perform for people.','Agreed. Enjoying his company would be quite enough.'],
      ['You could ask what he enjoys hearing.','That is much better. I occasionally need help turning enthusiasm into manners.']),
    t('Coming back for the company','At first I came here for songs. Now I miss the people when I am away.',
      ['Does that include me?','Yes. I was hoping that was apparent without making a speech, but I can make one if required.'],
      ['That is how places start feeling familiar.','Exactly. I know a few more names and want to hear how those people are doing.'],
      ['I am glad we met.','So am I. An excellent result for an evening I kept failing to leave.']));
  p('Vale','Reader and occasional traveller','Vale enjoys odd words, predictable comforts, and conversations that allow a person to choose what to reveal.',
    'Vale. I am happy to talk, provided neither of us is required to become instantly fascinating.',
    'A dragon. You have made an extremely strong opening argument for an interesting conversation.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I shall revise my expectations without assuming that makes every question polite.',
    'Corin. A familiar visitor is a pleasant interruption.',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. I learnt that when the dog attempted to adopt me for an afternoon.',
    t('A word with no use','I enjoy finding a word I have no reason to use. Then I spend a week attempting to create the reason.',
      ['Does that annoy your friends?','Occasionally. They have become skilled at asking what I actually mean.'],
      ['Why not just enjoy knowing it?','A sensible proposal. Apparently I want applause for having opened a book.'],
      ['What makes a good word?','One that says precisely what you need. The difficulty is admitting when a simpler one does it better.']),
    t('A reliable breakfast','I like eating a familiar breakfast while visiting somewhere unfamiliar. One part of the day need not be a discovery.',
      ['Do people call that unadventurous?','Yes. I invite them to have a more exciting breakfast and leave mine in peace.'],
      ['Would you ever try something new?','Gladly, once I have eaten. Hunger makes me a poor judge of novelty.'],
      ['I like familiar things on the road too.','Then we can enjoy that without forming a society to defend it.']),
    t('The question I declined','A stranger once asked a very personal question, then complained that I was unfriendly when I declined to answer.',
      ['What did you say?','That friendliness did not require me to provide every detail he fancied knowing.'],
      ['Were you rude about it?','Probably less graceful than I could have been. I still think the refusal was fair.'],
      ['You can tell me if I ask too much.','Thank you. I would prefer a small honest correction to a long silent resentment.']),
    t('Being interesting against your will','A dragon companion must make you interesting to strangers before you decide whether you want a conversation.',
      ['That can be tiring.','I imagine so. You may have an ordinary conversation with me if you like.'],
      ['I enjoy some of the attention.','Good. You are allowed to enjoy it sometimes without accepting it constantly.'],
      ['He attracts the attention more than I do.','Then I hope people give him the same courtesy they would want themselves.']),
    t('A comfortable exception','I am usually reluctant to have my day interrupted. Your visits have become a welcome exception.',
      ['That sounds almost affectionate.','A dangerous accusation, but I will not deny it.'],
      ['You can still tell me when you need quiet.','Thank you. An exception need not become an obligation.'],
      ['I like that I can relax around you.','Then we have found something useful to do with an ordinary conversation.']));
  p('Cerys','Student of people','Cerys enjoys lively discussions, has a sister at the school, and is learning to ask questions without treating people as puzzles.',
    'Hello, Cerys. If I ask too many questions, you can ask one back. That usually slows me down.',
    'A dragon! I was about to ask whether you had an interesting journey. I think I should choose a better question.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would like to hear your version before deciding what I think I know.',
    'Corin! You get the first question today, if you want it.',
    'That is Bramble, Rowan’s dog. He is much quicker at making friends than I am.',
    t('The person who surprised me','I mistook a very quiet woman for someone with nothing to say. Then she told the funniest story I heard all evening.',
      ['Why had she stayed quiet?','She said she was listening. I had been treating silence as a problem she needed to solve.'],
      ['Did you tell her you were surprised?','No. “I did not expect you to be interesting” makes a dreadful compliment.'],
      ['Did it change how you treat people?','I am trying to leave room before deciding who someone is.']),
    t('A disagreement with my sister','My sister and I once argued about whether I had interrupted her. I interrupted her explanation. The evidence was unusually clear.',
      ['Did you notice yourself doing it?','She waited until I finished, then raised one eyebrow. I understood.'],
      ['Did you apologise?','Yes, without adding a defence. That was the difficult part.'],
      ['Are you better at listening now?','Sometimes. I would like credit for improvement without claiming to be cured.']),
    t('Enjoying being wrong','I like guessing the end of a story and then being surprised by a better ending.',
      ['What makes an ending better?','It makes sense once it happens without being obvious beforehand. I dislike a surprise that simply ignores the story.'],
      ['Do you ever tell people your guess?','I am learning to ask whether they want to hear it. Apparently some people enjoy finding out in order.'],
      ['What if your guess was better?','Then I complain privately and enjoy my imaginary career as an author.']),
    t('Asking about friendship first','What do you enjoy about your dragon’s company when nothing dangerous is happening?',
      ['Having someone to share the day with.','That is a good answer. People ask about battles and forget the rest of the day exists.'],
      ['He can be funny when I least expect it.','I would much rather hear that than another claim about how terrifying dragons ought to be.'],
      ['I do not always know how to explain it.','You need not describe a friendship perfectly for it to be real.']),
    t('A question for me','You have answered enough questions. I owe you an honest answer of my own.',
      ['What are you looking forward to?','An evening with my sister when neither of us is trying to improve the other.'],
      ['Are you happy here?','Mostly. Wanting to see more of the world does not mean I dislike the place I am in.'],
      ['Have you enjoyed our conversations?','Yes. Including the moments when I had to stop and reconsider what I was asking.']));
  p('Nyra','Performer and card player','Nyra enjoys an agreed illusion, values an audience’s trust, and likes people who can laugh at a harmless surprise.',
    'Nyra. You can relax; anything I try to make disappear during this conversation will be my own property.',
    'A dragon! At last, something astonishing that I do not immediately want to explain as a trick.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I promise to enjoy the news without pretending I had guessed it already.',
    'Corin. It is good to see someone I do not need to impress before we can talk.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. The dog has an excellent nose and no interest in being misdirected.',
    t('The trick that failed','I once lost the coin I was supposed to make reappear. The audience enjoyed my search more than the trick.',
      ['Did you find it?','In my own sleeve, exactly where it belonged. I had become so flustered that I forgot the method.'],
      ['Could you pretend it was intentional?','I tried for about a breath. Then I laughed, and everyone relaxed.'],
      ['Did you keep that part in the performance?','No. Real embarrassment is difficult to reproduce and unpleasant to rehearse.']),
    t('An audience that knows the secret','Sometimes people know how a trick works and still enjoy it. Being fooled is only part of the pleasure.',
      ['What is the other part?','Watching someone do a difficult thing well and share the surprise generously.'],
      ['Do you mind if they explain it?','During the performance, yes. Afterwards, I appreciate being asked before my work becomes their announcement.'],
      ['I would want to learn the method.','That is fair. Curiosity becomes rude when it assumes it is owed an immediate answer.']),
    t('A game worth losing','I like playing against someone whose pleasure in winning does not depend on making me miserable.',
      ['Does Dain qualify?','More often than he used to. I am cautiously encouraged.'],
      ['Are you a good loser?','Usually. I reserve a small quantity of theatrical indignation for close games.'],
      ['I dislike being teased after losing.','Then say so. Good company can find a joke that everybody enjoys.']),
    t('Something truly extraordinary','Your companion gives people a chance to be astonished without anyone arranging it for them.',
      ['That does not make him a performance.','You are right. Wonder is something the observer feels, not a job the observed creature must do.'],
      ['Sometimes I am astonished myself.','I hope you get to enjoy that without having to explain it immediately.'],
      ['He would probably prefer a proper introduction.','Then that is what he deserves. I can be impressed and still have manners.']),
    t('Nothing to prove today','I enjoy talking with you without planning how to be clever. It is restful.',
      ['You do not have to entertain me.','I know. I am trying to let that knowledge affect how I behave.'],
      ['I like your cleverness too.','Thank you. It is nicer as something I can offer than something I must keep producing.'],
      ['I feel the same about being impressive.','Then let us have a comfortably unremarkable minute together.']));
  p('Maren','Innkeeper','Maren runs Thornwell’s inn with clear directions and an understanding that tired guests need choices they can understand.',
    'Welcome to Thornwell Inn. I am Maren. Tell me what you need before I bury you in directions.',
    'A dragon! I can welcome you both without pretending I have already thought through every practical detail.',
    'A dragon travels with you? Thank you for explaining. I would rather discuss what you need than make assumptions.',
    'Corin, welcome back. Have you found time to rest?',
    'Bramble belongs to Rowan the Hunter. People looking for Rowan often try the Copper Cup.',
    t('The guest who asked three times','A tired guest asked where the stairs were three times. I nearly became impatient, then realised he was struggling to hear me.',
      ['What did you do?','Spoke clearly and showed him the direction. Repeating myself more irritably would not have helped.'],
      ['Did he explain the problem?','Not until I gave him time. People do not always want to begin a visit by explaining a difficulty.'],
      ['I forget directions when I am tired.','Many people do. You are welcome to ask again.']),
    t('A promise the inn can keep','I would rather promise a straightforward welcome than describe every stay as unforgettable.',
      ['An uneventful night sounds pleasant.','Exactly. Most tired travellers want to sleep, not acquire a story.'],
      ['What makes a welcome straightforward?','Clear directions, clear expectations, and room to ask a question without feeling foolish.'],
      ['Do you ever want an adventure yourself?','Sometimes. Preferably after arranging someone to mind the inn.']),
    t('The guest who returned years later','Someone once returned after years away and expected me to remember a conversation I had completely forgotten.',
      ['Did you pretend to remember?','No. I asked them to remind me. They were pleased to tell it again.'],
      ['Were they disappointed?','For a moment. Honesty made the second conversation easier than a performance of recognition would have.'],
      ['It must be hard to remember everyone.','It is. I can still treat each person as worth my attention now.']),
    t('Finding rest for two','Does having your dragon nearby help you settle when you reach an unfamiliar place?',
      ['Usually. Familiar company helps.','I understand. A place can be new while the person sharing it makes it feel safer.'],
      ['Sometimes we need different things.','Then it helps to say so before either of you becomes too tired to discuss it kindly.'],
      ['I still have trouble relaxing.','That need not mean the welcome failed. It can take time to stop expecting the next problem.']),
    t('A person I do remember','You are no longer just a traveller I greeted. I find myself hoping your next journey goes well.',
      ['That means something to me.','I am glad. A welcome can become more personal without becoming more complicated.'],
      ['I hope things go well for you too.','Thank you. Most of my hopes concern ordinary days going smoothly, but they matter to me.'],
      ['I will try to visit when I can.','I would enjoy that. Make it a pleasure, not another obligation on your route.']));
  p('Celia','History enthusiast','Celia is interested in ordinary households, surprising friendships, and the details grand histories tend to overlook.',
    'Hello, I am Celia. If you have come to talk, I would welcome a reason to stop arguing with a book.',
    'A dragon! I shall need to set aside several opinions before beginning this conversation.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then I would rather learn what your days are like than tell you what I expect.',
    'Corin, hello. Is there something you have been wanting to talk about?',
    'Bramble is Rowan the Hunter’s dog. Ada knows his habits at least as well as Rowan does.',
    t('A history of neighbours','I read about two families who quarrelled for years and still helped each other during a flood.',
      ['Did the quarrel end?','No. That was what interested me. They did not have to settle everything before deciding to help.'],
      ['What had they argued about?','A boundary. The flood made its precise location temporarily difficult to defend.'],
      ['Would you have helped?','I hope so. It is easy to be generous while safely reading the question.']),
    t('The object that changed a story','An account described a woman as careless until a later page mentioned she had been caring for three sick relatives.',
      ['That changes how her day sounds.','Yes. The writer had included the criticism before deciding her circumstances mattered.'],
      ['Was the writer unfair on purpose?','I cannot tell. Unfairness does not require a carefully planned intention.'],
      ['I would have wanted to hear from her.','So would I. Sometimes the voice you most want is the one the record did not preserve.']),
    t('Something nobody asked me to learn','I can recite a list of obsolete household taxes. This skill has brought very little joy to gatherings.',
      ['Why did you learn it?','I was annoyed by a contradiction and followed it too far. That explains several of my interests.'],
      ['Could it ever be useful?','Perhaps. I am trying not to wish for a situation that would make it so.'],
      ['You can enjoy knowing something useless.','Thank you. I would still prefer to be invited to a second gathering.']),
    t('What stories overlook about riders','Accounts of riders spend pages on battles and scarcely mention how two companions learned to live together.',
      ['That part takes work too.','I imagine it does. Affection does not automatically arrange a whole day.'],
      ['Sometimes it is simply enjoyable.','That deserves recording as well. Not every ordinary moment needs a hidden lesson.'],
      ['I would rather live it than document everything.','Fair. Being interesting does not make your life public property.']),
    t('A conversation worth remembering','I am glad we have had time to become familiar. It is easy to know facts about someone without actually knowing them.',
      ['What helps you know a person?','Hearing what delights them, what annoys them, and what they choose not to say. Time helps too.'],
      ['I enjoy learning about you as well.','Then I promise not to make the tax list our only shared interest.'],
      ['I am still learning who I am on this journey.','You are allowed to change while people care about you. Friendship need not freeze a person in place.']));
  p('Orin','Thornwell gardener','Orin likes useful questions, careful planting, and visitors who do not pretend to recognise every plant.',
    'Orin. If you want to ask about the town, go ahead. I am better at directions than at guessing what people need.',
    'A dragon! I think that is the first time I have forgotten what I was saying halfway through my own name.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would rather meet him politely than pretend the news is ordinary.',
    'Corin. What have you been noticing on the road?',
    'That is Bramble, Rowan the Hunter’s dog. He has an excellent memory for people who stop to greet him.',
    t('The seed packet I trusted','I once planted what a seller promised was a small variety. It grew tall enough to shade everything around it.',
      ['Did you complain?','Yes. The seller had repeated a description without checking it. We both learned something inconvenient.'],
      ['Could you move the plants?','Some. Others stayed, and I changed the planting around them. Grumbling did not create more sunlight.'],
      ['Would you buy from them again?','If they admitted what they did not know. I do not require perfection; I require an honest answer.']),
    t('Working beside someone','I enjoy working with a person who does not need every quiet moment explained.',
      ['Do you prefer not to talk?','Sometimes. Other days I will discuss anything to avoid noticing how much weeding remains.'],
      ['How can someone tell?','They can ask. I ought to be capable of answering a simple question about my own mood.'],
      ['I like company even when we are quiet.','Then we would probably work together quite comfortably.']),
    t('The thing I grow for myself','I grow a small patch of flowers because I enjoy them. They are not part of a plan to impress anybody.',
      ['What do you like about them?','The colour changes as they open. It gives me a reason to pay attention to the same place twice.'],
      ['Do people offer advice anyway?','Constantly. I thank them and continue growing what I like.'],
      ['I would like something that is just for pleasure.','Then allow yourself something small. It need not wait until every other task is finished.']),
    t('A visitor with wings','Your dragon must experience a crowded place very differently from someone walking through it.',
      ['We try to give people and each other room.','I will do the same. An introduction need not require squeezing closer.'],
      ['He can decide what feels comfortable.','Of course. I should ask instead of arranging his experience for him.'],
      ['You seem to have thought about it.','Only because I would dislike strangers deciding how near they could stand to me.']),
    t('A road with familiar stops','It is good to become a person you recognise on the road, rather than another stranger giving directions.',
      ['That is how Thornwell feels to me now.','I am glad. A town is easier to care about once its people have names.'],
      ['I enjoy coming back.','Then the road has given you something besides distance.'],
      ['What would you like to know about my travels?','Something you enjoyed enough to notice twice. We hear plenty about the dangers.']));
  p('Isolde','Thornwell resident','Isolde grew up in Thornwell. She likes taking long walks, learning family recipes and finding company without making every visit an errand.',
    'Hello, I am Isolde. Are you finding your way through Thornwell, or taking a little time to meet people?',
    'Oh! A dragon. I was about to ask where you had walked from. I suppose I should ask whether you walked at all.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would like to hear how you met, if you feel like telling me.',
    'Hello again, Corin. I am glad you stopped.',
    'That is Bramble, Rowan the Hunter’s dog. Look for Rowan at the Copper Cup in northern Thornwell.',
    t('A walk that went wrong','My aunt once took me for a short walk. We missed a turning, crossed the same stream twice, and got home after supper.',
      ['Was she worried?','She admitted it when we got home. On the walk she kept asking me to notice things, so I would have something to do besides worry.'],
      ['Did you find the right turning next time?','Yes. She made me lead, with her checking the route. Knowing I could find it was better than being told never to go there again.'],
      ['That sounds like a very long short walk.','The family still calls it her short walk. She has stopped promising how long anything will take.']),
    t('Trying an old family recipe','My aunt made a berry drink after our summer walks. I have tried her recipe several times, but mine never tastes quite as I remember.',
      ['Have you asked her what is different?','She says I used to drink it when I was tired, thirsty and eight. Apparently those are difficult ingredients to replace.'],
      ['Does yours taste good anyway?','It does. I should probably enjoy it before giving it another examination.'],
      ['Nan has recipes I would like to learn.','Ask her to make one with you. I wish I had watched my aunt more carefully instead of arriving just in time to drink it.']),
    t('Getting to know a town','I used to feel I needed a reason to knock on a neighbour’s door. Then someone told me they would quite like a visitor who did not need a favour.',
      ['I feel awkward doing that too.','Try asking whether they have time. They can say no without it meaning you were wrong to ask.'],
      ['Did you start visiting more?','A little. Now we can sometimes sit quietly without my deciding the visit has failed.'],
      ['What do you talk about?','Ordinary things. A difficult day, a funny mistake, plans we might never carry out. It need not become an important occasion.']),
    t('A travelling companion','What does your dragon enjoy when you are not trying to reach the next place?',
      ['We are still finding that out.','Then leave a little time to find out. It is easy to learn what someone can do for you before learning what they like.'],
      ['He seems to enjoy exploring with me.','That sounds like a good reason to keep some of your stops unhurried.'],
      ['Sometimes we both just need a rest.','A shared rest counts as company. You need not invent an activity to deserve one.']),
    t('A familiar stop','I recognised you before I started wondering whether you needed directions. It is nice to have reached that point.',
      ['I hoped you would remember me.','I did. I wanted to hear how you were getting on, too.'],
      ['No directions today. Just a visit.','Then you have answered the question I keep forgetting I do not need to ask. Stay a while.'],
      ['I like coming back to familiar people.','So do I. Tell me something you enjoyed on the way, if you have a story to share.']));
  p('Cartwright Oswin','Cartwright','Oswin repairs carts, distrusts a hurried diagnosis, and enjoys a problem that can be understood by looking carefully.',
    'Oswin. I work on carts. You can still talk to me if you have arrived entirely on your own feet.',
    'A dragon! For once I shall not assume a traveller wants me to inspect a wheel.',
    'Your companion is a dragon? That changes my picture of your journey rather more than a different sort of cart would.',
    'Corin. Good to see you standing still long enough for a conversation.',
    'Rowan owns Bramble. The dog has supervised enough of my work to consider himself an expert.',
    t('The wheel that was not the problem','A driver asked for a new wheel because the cart pulled sideways. The load had been stacked badly; the wheel was sound.',
      ['Did that save much money?','Enough to make asking a few questions worthwhile. I dislike charging someone for the wrong repair.'],
      ['Were they embarrassed?','A little. I told them I had made the same mistake before learning to check.'],
      ['How do you start a repair?','By watching what is actually happening before deciding what ought to explain it.']),
    t('A tool with a history','I still use a tool my first teacher gave me. It is useful, but I admit I take better care of it because I know where it came from.',
      ['Did your teacher give many gifts?','Not many. That was part of why I understood the trust behind this one.'],
      ['Would you replace it if it broke?','I would repair it if possible. Keeping a memory does not require refusing to use anything else.'],
      ['Nan gave me things that matter that way.','Then you know the object carries more than its practical job, without making that job unimportant.']),
    t('A customer who stayed to learn','Someone asked to watch a repair instead of returning when it was finished. I enjoyed explaining it until I realised how often I said “obviously.”',
      ['Was it obvious?','Only after years of doing the work. I stopped using the word and became a clearer teacher.'],
      ['Did they learn to repair it themselves?','A simple part of it. Knowing enough to recognise a problem was useful too.'],
      ['Would you enjoy teaching more?','In manageable amounts. I would rather answer one person carefully than impress a crowd badly.']),
    t('Travelling under your own power','A dragon may spare you some problems with carts. I imagine he introduces several considerations I have never needed to make.',
      ['We still need rest and supplies.','Then the fundamentals remain stubbornly familiar, even with wings involved.'],
      ['He is a companion, not transport.','Quite right. I was comparing journeys and nearly forgot the person making yours with you.'],
      ['What would you ask us before offering advice?','What you actually need. That question has saved me a great many unnecessary explanations.']),
    t('A repair you did not need','I am glad some visitors come without something broken. It gives me a chance to know the person as well as the problem.',
      ['That is why I stopped.','Then you have made a pleasant change to the day.'],
      ['Do people usually only visit for work?','Often. It is understandable, but I enjoy having friends whose first sentence is not a diagnosis.'],
      ['What would you like to talk about?','Something you have learned to do that once seemed difficult. I enjoy hearing how people begin.']));
  p('Tessa','Travelling musician','Tessa is a musician visiting the Copper Cup. She enjoys adapting a performance to the people listening and is distinct from Tamsin at the school.',
    'Hello, I am Tessa. If you have come to discuss music, wonderful. If not, I am allowed interests between songs.',
    'A dragon! That is a sight I would struggle to describe in a song without sounding as though I had invented it.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would like to hear about the journey from you, before it acquires a chorus in somebody else’s telling.',
    'Corin! I am glad you found time to visit.',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. Bess can help you find him at the Copper Cup.',
    t('Changing the performance','I once prepared a lively set for a room full of exhausted travellers. They wanted something quiet. I nearly took that personally.',
      ['Did you change what you played?','Yes. I was there to share an evening, not to insist they have the mood I had rehearsed for.'],
      ['Was it difficult?','The playing was easier than accepting my splendid plan no longer suited anyone.'],
      ['Did they appreciate it?','They relaxed. That was a more useful response than applause would have been.']),
    t('A request from a child','A child asked whether I knew a song about a very specific frog. I had to admit my repertoire had a gap.',
      ['Did the child know the song?','No. They thought somebody ought to write it. I admired the confidence of the request.'],
      ['Did you invent one?','A short, extremely inaccurate account of a frog’s working day. The child corrected several details.'],
      ['Would you play it again?','For an audience prepared to take the frog’s responsibilities seriously.']),
    t('Practising where nobody listens','I enjoy practising a difficult phrase when nobody is waiting for me to get it right.',
      ['Does performing make it harder?','Sometimes. I try to remember the music instead of imagining everybody’s judgement.'],
      ['What if you never get it perfect?','Then I can still make it worth hearing. Perfection is not the only thing a listener enjoys.'],
      ['Do you get bored with repetition?','Yes. That is usually when a rest helps more than a fiftieth impatient attempt.']),
    t('A song you have not asked for','I will not turn you and your dragon into a song merely because I find your journey interesting.',
      ['Thank you for asking first.','It is your life. My interest does not automatically make it material I may borrow.'],
      ['A song might be enjoyable someday.','Then we can discuss it someday. There is no hurry to make you into a finished story.'],
      ['I would want him to have a say too.','Of course. A story about companions should listen to both of them.']),
    t('A familiar welcome on a visit','I have enjoyed getting to know you without needing to know the ending of your journey.',
      ['I do not know the ending either.','Then we can be interested in the day you are having. It is conveniently available.'],
      ['I am glad we can just talk.','So am I. Not every conversation needs to become a performance.'],
      ['What would make today good for you?','A little music, decent company, and no pressure to turn either into a grand occasion.']));
  p('Scholar Ilyan','Scholar of the desert','Ilyan studies the Sunken Pyramid west of Sandspire and the Emberheart relic described in its records. He is careful to distinguish an invitation from an obligation.',
    'I am Ilyan. I study the desert records here at Thornwell’s school. What brings you to the upper study?',
    'A dragon! My research concerns an old relic tied to dragon fire. I should introduce myself before treating this as a fortunate coincidence.',
    'You travel with a dragon? Then a discovery I have been studying may interest you, but it need not determine what we talk about.',
    'Corin, welcome. Have you come with a question, or simply for a visit?',
    'Bramble is Rowan the Hunter’s dog. I learned the name from people here in town.',
    t('A promising translation','I once translated a desert inscription as a warning about an ancient guardian. A colleague pointed out that it described a storekeeper.',
      ['How did you make that mistake?','The word meant someone who guarded a place. I supplied the grandeur myself.'],
      ['Were you disappointed?','Embarrassed first, then interested. Ordinary work had left a record worth understanding.'],
      ['How do you check a translation now?','Against other uses of the words, and with somebody who has not become attached to my first interpretation.']),
    t('Studying a place from far away','Being far from the desert helps me compare accounts. It also makes it easy to forget what the journey asks of a person.',
      ['Have you travelled there yourself?','I know the region better than the pyramid’s dangerous chambers. I must not let one claim stand in for the other.'],
      ['Why work in Thornwell?','The school gives me access to accounts collected from several routes. It is a useful place to ask questions together.'],
      ['Could advice from here still help?','Yes, if I state its limits. Useful information does not need to pretend it is complete.']),
    t('Who an expedition is for','Scholars can become so excited about a discovery that the people taking the risk seem like a means of answering a question.',
      ['How do you avoid that?','By accepting a refusal and making the danger clear. Wanting knowledge does not entitle me to someone else’s journey.'],
      ['Would you take the same risk?','Not with my present abilities. That is a reason to be modest about asking another person to consider it.'],
      ['I can decide what I am ready for.','Yes. I can offer information without deciding your courage on your behalf.']),
    t('A companion before a discovery','Your dragon matters to you as a friend. I must remember that before discussing what my research could teach us about him.',
      ['He can decide what he wants to share.','Then that decision belongs in the conversation before any clever question of mine.'],
      ['I am curious about dragon fire too.','Good. Curiosity we share can become a discussion rather than an examination.'],
      ['Some days we want to be ordinary travellers.','You are welcome here on those days as well. I can put the research aside.']),
    t('News that need not be a report','You may visit without bringing evidence from a ruin. I would like to know how you are doing.',
      ['I appreciate being asked that first.','I am glad. Research is what I work on; it need not be all I notice about a friend.'],
      ['I do have questions about the road.','Then we can look at them. Choosing to discuss work is different from being expected to supply it.'],
      ['How is your own work going?','Slowly, with fewer imaginary guardians in the translations. I consider that progress.']));
  p('Eira','Cider maker','Eira likes testing her own ideas, dislikes elaborate praise that tells her nothing, and enjoys an evening with no work to sell.',
    'Hello, I am Eira. I make cider, though I am quite happy to talk about something that does not involve apples.',
    'A dragon! I was expecting a traveller with a question, and you have supplied me with several of my own.',
    'You travel with a dragon? I would rather hear how that feels than invent a dramatic explanation for it.',
    'Corin. Good to see you taking a moment for yourself.',
    'That is Rowan’s dog, Bramble. His owner is a regular at the Copper Cup.',
    t('The batch nobody could agree on','I make cider, and I asked four neighbours to taste a new batch. I received five opinions; one changed his mind halfway through explaining.',
      ['Was any of the advice useful?','The person who said it was too sweet gave me something I could actually test. “Interesting” was considerably less helpful.'],
      ['Did you change the recipe?','For one small batch. I wanted to compare the results, not surrender the entire recipe to a committee.'],
      ['Perhaps they just liked different things.','They did. That was the useful conclusion I nearly missed while trying to make everybody agree.']),
    t('An evening away from work','I like an evening when nobody asks me to judge what they are drinking. I can have preferences without being on duty.',
      ['What would you rather talk about?','Which person in Thornwell would survive longest if everybody had to swap occupations for a day.'],
      ['Would you mind if I asked about your work another time?','Not at all. I am allowed to enjoy discussing it as well as occasionally wanting a change.'],
      ['Whose occupation would you choose?','Linnet’s, for the alarming hour before everybody discovered I cannot play.']),
    t('A celebration that was not mine','I once helped prepare a celebration and became absurdly annoyed when nobody noticed one detail I had worked hard on.',
      ['Did you tell them?','No. I went home, complained to myself, and eventually remembered whose celebration it had been.'],
      ['It still hurts to feel overlooked.','It does. I could acknowledge that without making the whole occasion responsible for it.'],
      ['Did they enjoy the celebration?','Very much. I am now willing to count that as the intended result.']),
    t('Making room for surprise','Are you still surprised to find yourself travelling with a dragon, or has it started feeling ordinary?',
      ['Both, at different moments.','I like that answer. Something can become familiar without becoming unremarkable.'],
      ['Sometimes I forget how startling it is to other people.','Then I apologise in advance for the occasional foolish expression. Surprise takes a moment to acquire manners.'],
      ['I am mostly glad of his company.','That seems a better foundation for a journey than trying to stay astonished every minute.']),
    t('The pleasure of a repeat visit','I was pleased when I realised I recognised you. It is nice to have a conversation that can continue becoming a friendship.',
      ['I have enjoyed our talks.','Then neither of us has been politely enduring the other. A reassuring discovery.'],
      ['What would make today a good visit?','A little news, a little nonsense, and neither of us pretending we are less tired than we are.'],
      ['I hope I can keep coming back.','So do I. There is no need to make a promise about exactly when.']));
  p('Fenton','Traveller and storyteller','Fenton likes an entertaining account, including one that admits the teller was not the most competent person present.',
    'Fenton. I enjoy a story, but you are welcome to introduce yourself without bringing one.',
    'A dragon! I should retire my claim that I have met every sort of traveller on this road.',
    'You travel with a dragon? That is news worth hearing without adding anything to it.',
    'Corin! How has the road treated you since we last spoke?',
    'Rowan the Hunter owns Bramble. The dog has tried to extend several of my visits by leaning against my legs.',
    t('The inn I walked past','I spent an hour looking for an inn I had already walked past. I was so certain it ought to look grander that I ignored the sign.',
      ['Who finally pointed it out?','A child who asked whether I had tried reading the building. A devastatingly practical suggestion.'],
      ['Was it comfortable?','Very. I slept without requiring the roof to apologise for its appearance.'],
      ['Did you admit how long you had been searching?','Eventually. The innkeeper was kind enough to wait before laughing.']),
    t('A story with someone else as the hero','My best travel story features a stranger who got me out of trouble. For years I made my own mistake the smallest part of the account.',
      ['What mistake?','I ignored a warning because I thought the speaker looked inexperienced. She knew that road; I knew how to sound confident.'],
      ['Did you thank her?','Yes. I should have listened to her before I needed rescuing, but gratitude was still available afterwards.'],
      ['Do you tell the whole version now?','I try. It gives the story a useful subject besides my narrow escape.']),
    t('A destination chosen for pleasure','I once travelled simply because I wanted to hear a particular musician. People kept asking what the real reason was.',
      ['Was the performance worth it?','Yes. So was the anticipation. The journey did not need a more important excuse.'],
      ['Would you do it again?','If I could arrange the time. Pleasure still has to fit around the people depending on me.'],
      ['I would enjoy choosing a journey like that.','Then keep the idea. Not every road needs to begin with something going wrong.']),
    t('Who gets the exciting parts?','When people hear about you and your dragon, do they leave you any room to describe an uneventful afternoon?',
      ['Not always.','That is a shame. Sometimes the best part is that everybody ate, rested, and remained on speaking terms.'],
      ['You like an exciting account yourself.','Guilty. I am trying to remember it is more pleasant to hear about trouble than to be in it.'],
      ['I do enjoy telling some of the stories.','Then tell the ones you want to tell. You do not owe an audience your worst moment.']),
    t('Someone worth meeting again','I look forward to your visits, even when you have nothing to report.',
      ['That is good to know.','It is good to say. I sometimes hide simple affection inside an unnecessarily long story.'],
      ['I might still have a story for you.','Then I shall listen with pleasure and a reasonable number of interruptions.'],
      ['Have you had a good day?','Better now that someone has asked without needing directions first.']));
  return cast;
})();
